/* Power Up — questions en anglais (cyber). Clé = question française + « ¦ » + première réponse. */
PU_I18N.questions({
  "Les trois piliers de la sécurité de l'information (triade DIC) : ¦ Disponibilité, Intégrité, Confidentialité": {"q":"The three pillars of information security (the CIA triad, called DIC in French):","e":"Available when you need it, intact (not altered), confidential (seen only by the right people). In French: DIC. Encryption or identification are means, not pillars.","a":["Availability, Integrity, Confidentiality","Availability, Identification, Encryption","Detection, Integrity, Compliance"]},
  "Que signifie ANSSI ? ¦ Agence nationale de la sécurité des systèmes d'information": {"q":"What does ANSSI stand for?","e":"ANSSI is the French cybersecurity authority. It publishes very useful IT hygiene guides, free of charge and in French.","a":["National Agency for the Security of Information Systems","National Association of IT Services","National Authority for Internet Site Surveillance"]},
  "Une fuite de données personnelles présente un risque pour les personnes. Selon le RGPD, il faut prévenir la CNIL… ¦ Dans les 72 heures après en avoir pris connaissance": {"q":"A personal data breach poses a risk to individuals. Under the GDPR, you must notify the CNIL…","e":"The GDPR requires notifying the supervisory authority (the CNIL in France) within 72 hours, and informing the individuals concerned if the risk is high. The 24 hours is the NIS 2 early warning.","a":["Within 72 hours of becoming aware of it","Within 24 hours of discovering the breach","Within the following month, once the investigation is complete"]},
  "Le RGPD protège… ¦ Les mots de passe Wi-Fi de mamie": {"q":"The GDPR protects…","e":"The General Data Protection Regulation has applied since 2018 across the European Union, to any organization that processes people's data.","a":["Grandma's Wi-Fi passwords","Companies' trade secrets","People's personal data"]},
  "La charte informatique d'une entreprise… ¦ Fixe les règles d'usage du numérique que chacun s'engage à respecter": {"q":"A company's IT charter…","e":"Passwords, personal use, data, possible sanctions… It is often appended to the internal regulations and signed on arrival.","a":["Sets the rules for using digital tools that everyone agrees to follow","Describes the network architecture and the firewall rules","Sets the mandatory dress code for Teams meetings"]},
  "Le nom, l'adresse mail professionnelle et l'adresse IP peuvent être des données personnelles. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A name, a work email address and an IP address can be personal data.","e":"True: any information that can identify a person, directly or indirectly, is personal data, even in a professional context."},
  "La CNIL, c'est… ¦ L'agence nationale chargée de la cybersécurité de l'État": {"q":"The CNIL is…","e":"It advises, audits and can impose sanctions. It is also the body you notify of a personal data breach. State cybersecurity is the role of the ANSSI.","a":["The national agency in charge of the State's cybersecurity","The French personal data protection authority","The police unit specialized in cybercrime"]},
  "La directive européenne NIS 2… ¦ Encadre la résilience numérique du seul secteur financier": {"q":"The European NIS 2 directive…","e":"Healthcare, energy, transport, local authorities, digital providers (including managed service providers)… Thousands of French organizations are concerned, under the ANSSI's aegis. The financial sector also has its own regulation: DORA.","a":["Governs digital resilience of the financial sector only","Only concerns operators of vital importance (OIV)","Extends cybersecurity obligations to many more organizations"]},
  "Le principe de « minimisation » du RGPD, c'est… ¦ Ne collecter que les données strictement nécessaires à l'objectif": {"q":"The GDPR principle of “minimization” is…","e":"Less data collected = fewer risks in case of a leak. A newsletter sign-up form doesn't need a date of birth. The retention period falls under another principle: storage limitation.","a":["Collecting only the data strictly necessary for the purpose","Reducing the retention period to the strict legal minimum","Pseudonymizing data as soon as it is collected"]},
  "ISO/IEC 27001 est… ¦ Un guide de bonnes pratiques détaillant les mesures de sécurité": {"q":"ISO/IEC 27001 is…","e":"It requires a continuous improvement approach: risk analysis, security controls, audits. A reassuring certification for an MSP's customers. The guide to controls is ISO 27002.","a":["A best-practice guide detailing security controls","An international standard for security management (ISMS)","A European cybersecurity regulation for companies"]},
  "Un DPO (délégué à la protection des données)… ¦ Pilote la sécurité technique du SI et ses équipes": {"q":"A DPO (data protection officer)…","e":"It is mandatory for public bodies and for some companies. The DPO is the point of contact for the CNIL and for the individuals concerned, without representing the CNIL. Technical security is the role of the CISO (RSSI).","a":["Leads the technical security of the IT system and its teams","Represents the CNIL within the organization","Advises the organization and monitors its GDPR compliance"]},
  "EBIOS Risk Manager est… ¦ Une méthode d'analyse des risques cyber publiée par l'ANSSI": {"q":"EBIOS Risk Manager is…","e":"It starts from realistic attack scenarios (who could attack us, how, and for what purpose?) to choose the most useful security measures.","a":["A cyber risk analysis method published by the ANSSI","A certifiable security controls framework published by ISO","An IT hygiene guide with 42 measures from the ANSSI"]},
  "Que trouve-t-on dans une PSSI (politique de sécurité du système d'information) ? ¦ Les objectifs et les règles de sécurité": {"q":"What can be found in a PSSI (information system security policy)?","e":"The PSSI is the reference security document; the IT charter is its translation for users. It sets rules, never the secrets themselves.","a":["Security objectives and rules","Roles and responsibilities","Administrator account passwords","Access management rules"]},
  "Sous NIS 2, un incident important doit faire l'objet d'une alerte précoce… ¦ Dans les 72 heures": {"q":"Under NIS 2, a significant incident must be the subject of an early warning…","e":"Early warning within 24 h, detailed notification within 72 h, final report within one month.","a":["Within 72 hours","Within 24 hours","Within 7 days"]},
  "Le règlement européen DORA concerne surtout… ¦ La sécurité des produits connectés vendus dans l'UE": {"q":"The European DORA regulation mainly concerns…","e":"Banks, insurers and their critical IT providers: risk management, resilience testing, incident reporting. Applicable since January 2025. Connected products fall under the Cyber Resilience Act.","a":["The security of connected products sold in the EU","The protection of banks' customer data","The digital operational resilience of the financial sector"]},
  "La qualification SecNumCloud de l'ANSSI atteste… ¦ Qu'un service cloud atteint un haut niveau de sécurité, à l'abri des lois extra-européennes": {"q":"The ANSSI's SecNumCloud qualification certifies…","e":"It is required to host certain sensitive State data and data of operators of vital importance.","a":["That a cloud service reaches a high level of security, protected from non-European laws","That a cloud service complies with the GDPR and has been certified by the CNIL","That a cloud provider is ISO 27001 certified by an accredited body"]},
  "Quel article du RGPD impose de notifier une violation de données personnelles à l'autorité de contrôle (la CNIL) ? ¦ 33": {"q":"Which article of the GDPR requires notifying a personal data breach to the supervisory authority (the CNIL)?","e":"Article 33 requires notifying the CNIL within 72 hours, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk; Article 34 deals with informing individuals. The Commission's “Digital Omnibus” proposal (November 2025) plans to move to 96 hours and to limit notification to high risk, but it has not been adopted: 72 hours remains the rule.","placeholder":"Article number","answers":["33","article 33","art. 33","art 33"]},
  "Depuis le 11 septembre 2026, le Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) oblige les fabricants à envoyer une alerte précoce sur une vulnérabilité activement exploitée de leur produit. En combien d'heures au maximum ? ¦ 24": {"q":"Since 11 September 2026, the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) requires manufacturers to send an early warning about an actively exploited vulnerability in their product. Within how many hours at most?","e":"CRA Article 14: early warning within 24 h, notification within 72 h, then a final report no later than 14 days after a corrective measure is made available. Reporting goes through ENISA's single reporting platform, to the coordinating CSIRT (CERT-FR in France).","placeholder":"Number of hours","answers":["24","24h","24 h","24 heures","24 hours","24 hrs","24hrs"]},
  "Tu dois transmettre un fichier de données clients à un partenaire. Le bon réflexe ? ¦ L'envoyer depuis ta messagerie personnelle, c'est plus simple": {"q":"You need to send a customer data file to a partner. What is the right reflex?","e":"Personal data must stay in controlled and traceable tools. Restricted sharing (ideally with an expiry date) limits the damage if the wrong recipient is chosen.","a":["Send it from your personal email, it's simpler","Upload it to a free file-sharing site found online","Use the approved sharing tool, with access limited to the recipient"]},
  "Une amende RGPD peut atteindre 20 millions d'euros ou 4 % du chiffre d'affaires annuel mondial, le montant le plus élevé étant retenu. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A GDPR fine can reach 20 million euros or 4% of annual worldwide turnover, whichever is higher.","e":"True: this is the ceiling for the most serious infringements (principles, individuals' rights, transfers). Other infringements are capped at €10M or 2%."},
  "Selon le RGPD, une analyse d'impact (AIPD) est obligatoire quand un traitement… ¦ Porte sur les données de plus de 5 000 personnes": {"q":"According to the GDPR, an impact assessment (DPIA) is mandatory when a processing operation…","e":"Large-scale monitoring, sensitive data, profiling… The CNIL publishes the list of processing operations for which a DPIA is required, and offers a free tool (PIA) to carry it out.","a":["Concerns the data of more than 5,000 people","Is likely to result in a high risk for individuals","Transfers data outside the European Union"]},
  "Dans un SMSI ISO 27001, la déclaration d'applicabilité (DdA, ou SoA)… ¦ Liste les mesures de l'annexe A retenues ou exclues, avec leur justification": {"q":"In an ISO 27001 ISMS, the Statement of Applicability (SoA)…","e":"It is a central audit document: it links the risk analysis to the chosen controls and explains each exclusion.","a":["Lists the Annex A controls selected or excluded, with their justification","Is the certificate of conformity issued by the audit body","Describes the scope of the ISMS (sites, activities, systems covered)"]},
  "Sous NIS 2, après l'alerte précoce envoyée sous 24 h, quelles sont les échéances suivantes ? ¦ Notification d'incident sous 7 jours, rapport final sous 3 mois": {"q":"Under NIS 2, after the early warning sent within 24 h, what are the next deadlines?","e":"The scheme has three stages: early warning (24 h), notification with an initial severity assessment and IOCs (72 h), final report (1 month). An interim report may be requested in the meantime.","a":["Incident notification within 7 days, final report within 3 months","Incident notification within 72 h, final report no later than one month after","Incident notification within 48 h, final report within 6 months"]},
  "Dans ISO/IEC 27001:2022, l'annexe A contient… ¦ 114 mesures réparties en 14 domaines": {"q":"In ISO/IEC 27001:2022, Annex A contains…","e":"The 4 themes: organizational, people, physical and technological. The 2013 version had 114 controls in 14 domains; the 2022 revision merged some and added 11, including threat intelligence and cloud security.","a":["114 controls in 14 domains","120 controls in 6 chapters","93 controls in 4 themes"]},
  "Depuis quand le RGPD s'applique-t-il dans toute l'Union européenne ? ¦ Depuis le 1er janvier 2016": {"q":"Since when has the GDPR applied across the European Union?","e":"The GDPR, adopted in 2016, has been applicable since 25 May 2018. 17 October 2024 is the NIS 2 transposition deadline.","a":["Since 1 January 2016","Since 25 May 2018","Since 1 January 2020","Since 17 October 2024"]},
  "Un client te demande quelles données l'entreprise détient sur lui. Il exerce son… ¦ droit d'opposition": {"q":"A customer asks you what data the company holds about them. They are exercising their…","e":"The right of access allows anyone to obtain a copy of their data and information about how it is processed. Rectification is used to correct inaccurate data.","a":["right to object","right to data portability","right of access","right to rectification"]},
  "Le RGPD ne s'applique qu'aux entreprises de plus de 250 salariés. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The GDPR only applies to companies with more than 250 employees.","e":"False: the GDPR applies to any organization that processes personal data, whatever its size, including associations and very small businesses. Only a few obligations (such as the register) are relaxed in some cases."},
  "Sur un formulaire web, une case « J'accepte de recevoir la newsletter » déjà cochée par défaut constitue un consentement valable. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"On a web form, an “I agree to receive the newsletter” checkbox that is ticked by default constitutes valid consent.","e":"False: consent must result from a clear affirmative act by the person. A pre-ticked box does not prove that the person really agreed."},
  "Quelles informations sont des données personnelles ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le numéro de téléphone professionnel d'un salarié": {"q":"Which pieces of information are personal data? (several answers)","e":"Personal data can identify a natural person, directly or indirectly: phone number, license plate, photo. A company's turnover concerns a legal entity.","a":["An employee's work phone number","A car's license plate","A company's overall turnover","A colleague's photo on the intranet"]},
  "Quel est le sigle du règlement européen sur la protection des données personnelles ? ¦ RGPD": {"q":"What is the acronym of the European regulation on personal data protection?","e":"GDPR stands for “General Data Protection Regulation” (RGPD in French). It is a regulation: it applies directly in all EU countries.","placeholder":"4-letter acronym","answers":["RGPD","GDPR"]},
  "Laquelle de ces données est une donnée « sensible » au sens du RGPD ? ¦ L'adresse postale personnelle d'un client": {"q":"Which of these data is “sensitive” data under the GDPR?","e":"Health data is one of the special categories (along with racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious beliefs, biometrics…), whose processing is in principle prohibited except in certain cases.","a":["A customer's personal postal address","An employee's hiring date and job title","The access badge number for the premises","Information about an employee's health"]},
  "Un collègue t'avoue avoir envoyé par erreur le fichier des salaires à un destinataire externe. Ton réflexe ? ¦ Prévenir tout de suite ton responsable ou le DPO": {"q":"A colleague admits to having mistakenly sent the salary file to an external recipient. What is your reflex?","e":"This is a personal data breach: the company must assess it quickly, because a notification to the CNIL may be required within a short deadline. Hiding the incident wastes precious time.","a":["Immediately tell your manager or the DPO","Wait and see whether the recipient reacts","Delete the email from their sent items and say nothing","Ask the recipient to forward it to the right person"]},
  "Le registre des activités de traitement exigé par le RGPD recense… ¦ la liste des incidents de sécurité survenus dans l'année": {"q":"The record of processing activities required by the GDPR lists…","e":"The record describes each personal data processing activity of the organization: purpose, categories of data and individuals, recipients, retention periods, security measures… Incidents are recorded elsewhere, in the breach register (or documentation).","a":["the security incidents that occurred during the year","each processing activity, with its purpose, data and recipients","the accounts and access rights to the personal databases","the names of the people who gave consent, with the date"]},
  "Quelles bases légales sont prévues par le RGPD pour traiter des données ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le consentement de la personne": {"q":"Which legal bases does the GDPR provide for processing data? (several answers)","e":"The GDPR provides six legal bases: consent, contract, legal obligation, protection of vital interests, public interest task and legitimate interest. The length of a relationship is not one of them.","a":["The person's consent","Performance of a contract","The length of the customer relationship","The legitimate interest of the controller"]},
  "Un sous-traitant au sens du RGPD (par exemple un prestataire cloud) n'a aucune obligation propre : seul son client est responsable. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A processor under the GDPR (for example a cloud provider) has no obligations of its own: only its customer is responsible.","e":"False: the processor must notably secure the data, act only on the customer's instructions, alert them in case of a breach and keep its own register. It can also be sanctioned."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes de la roue de Deming (PDCA), base classique de l'amélioration continue d'un SMSI : ¦ Planifier (Plan)": {"q":"Put in order the steps of the Deming wheel (PDCA), the classic basis for the continuous improvement of an ISMS:","e":"You plan (risks, objectives), implement the controls, check (audits, indicators), then correct and improve, before starting a new cycle.","items":["Plan","Do","Check","Act"]},
  "La « protection des données dès la conception » (privacy by design) signifie… ¦ faire valider chaque nouveau projet par la CNIL avant son lancement": {"q":"“Data protection by design” (privacy by design) means…","e":"The GDPR requires data protection to be considered by design, then by default (collect only what is necessary). No systematic prior validation by the CNIL is required.","a":["having every new project validated by the CNIL before launch","encrypting data only once the application is in production","building data protection in from the start of a project, not as an afterthought","entrusting the design of all projects to the DPO"]},
  "Comment appelle-t-on le fait de remplacer le nom d'une personne par un identifiant (code, alias), les données restant personnelles car la correspondance peut être retrouvée ? ¦ pseudonymisation": {"q":"What do we call replacing a person's name with an identifier (code, alias), where the data remains personal because the match can be recovered?","e":"Pseudonymization reduces risks, but the data remains subject to the GDPR since the person can be re-identified using the mapping table. Anonymization, on the other hand, makes re-identification impossible and takes the data out of the GDPR's scope.","placeholder":"One word…","answers":["pseudonymisation","pseudonymisation des données","pseudonymiser","pseudonymization","pseudonymize","pseudonymise"]},
  "À quoi servent les clauses contractuelles types (CCT, ou SCC) adoptées par la Commission européenne ? ¦ À encadrer un transfert de données hors UE sans décision d'adéquation": {"q":"What are the standard contractual clauses (SCCs) adopted by the European Commission used for?","e":"SCCs are a tool for transfers outside the EU: the exporter and the importer commit contractually. They often have to be supplemented by an analysis of the law of the destination country.","a":["To govern a transfer of data outside the EU without an adequacy decision","To replace the record of processing for small organizations","To exempt a processor from notifying data breaches","To certify the GDPR compliance of a European cloud provider"]},
  "Quelles catégories d'entités la directive NIS 2 définit-elle ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les entités essentielles": {"q":"Which categories of entities does the NIS 2 directive define? (several answers)","e":"NIS 2 distinguishes essential entities (EE) and important entities (IE). Operators of essential services (OES) came under NIS 1, and OIV is a separate French scheme.","a":["Essential entities","Important entities","Operators of essential services","Operators of vital importance"]},
  "Quelle est la différence entre ISO/IEC 27001 et ISO/IEC 27002 ? ¦ 27002 fixe les exigences certifiables, 27001 en est le guide d'application": {"q":"What is the difference between ISO/IEC 27001 and ISO/IEC 27002?","e":"You get certified against ISO 27001 (ISMS requirements). ISO 27002 details, control by control, how to apply the Annex A controls; it is not certifiable.","a":["27002 sets the certifiable requirements, 27001 is the implementation guide","27001 sets the certifiable ISMS requirements, 27002 guides the controls","27001 covers traditional IT, 27002 covers the cloud and industrial systems","Both are certifiable, 27002 being the lightweight version for SMEs"]},
  "Lorsqu'elle est obligatoire, l'AIPD doit être réalisée avant la mise en œuvre du traitement. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"When it is mandatory, the DPIA must be carried out before the processing is implemented.","e":"True: the impact assessment is prior. It is used to identify risks to individuals and to plan measures before launching the processing, and it is then reviewed if the processing changes."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le cycle d'une certification ISO/IEC 27001 : ¦ Audit initial étape 1 (revue documentaire)": {"q":"Put in order the cycle of an ISO/IEC 27001 certification:","e":"The initial audit takes place in two stages, then the certificate, valid for three years, is maintained by annual surveillance audits before a renewal audit.","items":["Initial audit stage 1 (documentation review)","Initial audit stage 2 (ISMS effectiveness)","Issuance of the certificate for three years","Annual surveillance audits","Renewal audit"]},
  "Quel article du RGPD impose de tenir un registre des activités de traitement ? ¦ 30": {"q":"Which article of the GDPR requires keeping a record of processing activities?","e":"Article 30 of the GDPR details the content of the record, for the controller as well as for the processor.","placeholder":"Article number","answers":["30","article 30","art. 30","art 30"]},
  "Sous DORA, le « registre d'informations » que doit tenir une entité financière recense… ¦ les incidents cyber majeurs notifiés au régulateur": {"q":"Under DORA, the “register of information” that a financial entity must keep lists…","e":"DORA requires documenting all contracts with third-party ICT providers in a register of information, which the authorities can request. It is the basis of third-party risk management.","a":["the major cyber incidents reported to the regulator","the results of threat-led penetration tests (TLPT)","all contractual arrangements with its third-party ICT service providers","the privileged accounts of its information system"]},
  "Dans une démarche RGPD, la « durée de conservation » d'un traitement doit être… ¦ illimitée tant que les données restent chiffrées et sécurisées": {"q":"In a GDPR approach, the “retention period” of a processing operation must be…","e":"The storage limitation principle requires a period proportionate to the purpose (sometimes set by law), followed by deletion, anonymization or intermediate archiving with restricted access.","a":["unlimited as long as the data remains encrypted and secured","set at 10 years for all processing, like accounting documents","left to each user's discretion, case by case","set according to the purpose, then followed by deletion or archiving"]},
  "Laquelle de ces mesures est apparue comme nouvelle dans ISO/IEC 27002:2022 ? ¦ Politique de contrôle d'accès (gestion des droits)": {"q":"Which of these controls appeared as new in ISO/IEC 27002:2022?","e":"The 2022 version added 11 controls, including threat intelligence, cloud services security, data masking and secure coding. The other three already existed in the 2013 version.","a":["Access control policy (rights management)","Information backup (copies and restore tests)","Segregation of duties (four-eyes principle)","Threat intelligence"]},
  "Les organismes certifiés ISO/IEC 27001:2013 avaient jusqu'au 31 octobre 2025 pour passer à la version 2022. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Organizations certified to ISO/IEC 27001:2013 had until 31 October 2025 to move to the 2022 version.","e":"True: the transition period set by the IAF was three years after the October 2022 publication. Since then, 2013 certificates are no longer valid."},
  "Un manquement du responsable de traitement à son obligation de sécurité (et non aux grands principes du RGPD) est plafonné à… ¦ 20 M€ ou 4 % du chiffre d'affaires annuel mondial": {"q":"A controller's failure to meet its security obligation (and not the GDPR's main principles) is capped at…","e":"The GDPR provides two tiers: €10M or 2% for the obligations of the controller and processor (security, register, DPIA…), €20M or 4% for the principles, legal bases, individuals' rights and transfers.","a":["€20M or 4% of annual worldwide turnover","€10M or 2% of annual worldwide turnover","€7M or 1.4% of annual worldwide turnover","€5M or 1% of annual worldwide turnover"]},
  "Sous NIS 2, quel montant maximal d'amende les États doivent-ils au moins prévoir pour une entité essentielle ? ¦ 7 M€ ou 1,4 % du chiffre d'affaires annuel mondial": {"q":"Under NIS 2, what maximum fine amount must Member States provide for at least for an essential entity?","e":"NIS 2 sets at least €10M or 2% of worldwide turnover for essential entities and €7M or 1.4% for important entities, whichever is higher. The €20M / 4% is the GDPR's upper ceiling.","a":["€7M or 1.4% of annual worldwide turnover","€20M or 4% of annual worldwide turnover","€10M or 2% of annual worldwide turnover","€15M or 3% of annual worldwide turnover"]},
  "En combien de mois au maximum (hors prolongation) dois-tu répondre à une demande d'exercice de droits RGPD ? ¦ 1": {"q":"Within how many months at most (excluding extension) must you respond to a request to exercise GDPR rights?","e":"The response deadline is one month from receipt of the request. It can be extended by two months if the request is complex or if there are many requests, provided the person is informed.","placeholder":"Number of months","answers":["1","un","1 mois","un mois","one","1 month","one month"]},
  "Une violation présente un risque élevé pour les personnes. Dans quels cas l'article 34 du RGPD dispense-t-il de les informer individuellement ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les données étaient chiffrées et la clé n'a pas été compromise": {"q":"A breach poses a high risk to individuals. In which cases does Article 34 of the GDPR exempt you from informing them individually? (several answers)","e":"Article 34 provides three exceptions: data rendered unintelligible, subsequent measures eliminating the high risk, disproportionate effort (with public communication). Notifying the CNIL never exempts you from informing individuals.","a":["The data was encrypted and the key was not compromised","Measures taken afterwards make the high risk unlikely","Individual notification would involve disproportionate effort (a public communication replaces it)","The CNIL was notified within 72 hours"]},
  "Un ransomware chiffre tes fichiers puis réclame une rançon. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Ransomware encrypts your files and then demands a ransom.","e":"True. And it often steals the data before encrypting it too (double extortion). Offline backups remain the best defense."},
  "Le Wi-Fi public d'un café est aussi sûr que le réseau de l'entreprise. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A café's public Wi-Fi is as safe as the company network.","e":"False: anyone can connect to it, or even create a fake access point with the same name. On a public network, use the company VPN or your phone's hotspot."},
  "Tu trouves une clé USB sur le parking de l'entreprise. Tu… ¦ La branches pour retrouver son propriétaire": {"q":"You find a USB drive in the company parking lot. You…","e":"Dropping booby-trapped drives is a well-known attack technique: all it takes is one curious person plugging it in. Even a scan is not enough: some drives pose as a keyboard as soon as they are plugged in. You never plug in an unknown device.","a":["Plug it in to find its owner","Hand it to the IT department without plugging it in","Plug it in, but only after an antivirus scan"]},
  "Lesquels sont des logiciels malveillants ? ¦ Un rançongiciel (ransomware)": {"q":"Which of these are malware?","e":"Ransomware, Trojan horses (which pose as a legitimate program) and worms (which spread on their own) are malware. A honeypot, on the other hand, is a decoy set up by defenders to observe attackers.","a":["Ransomware","A Trojan horse","A worm","A honeypot"]},
  "Le principe « Zero Trust », c'est… ¦ Ne jamais faire confiance par défaut, et vérifier chaque accès (identité, appareil, contexte)": {"q":"The “Zero Trust” principle means…","e":"Being on the company network is no longer enough: every access is verified, with the minimum necessary rights, on the assumption that a breach is possible.","a":["Never trusting by default, and verifying every access (identity, device, context)","Trusting the internal network and strictly filtering what comes from the Internet","Granting lasting access as soon as the device is enrolled and compliant"]},
  "Un cheval de Troie, c'est… ¦ Un malware qui se propage tout seul de machine en machine": {"q":"A Trojan horse is…","e":"As in the legend: you install it yourself, believing it is harmless (fake video player, “cracked” software…), and it opens the door for the attacker.","a":["Malware that spreads on its own from machine to machine","Software that looks useful but hides a malicious function","A wooden horse delivered to reception by mistake"]},
  "Un Mac ou un smartphone ne peut pas être infecté par un logiciel malveillant. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A Mac or a smartphone cannot be infected by malware.","e":"False: macOS, Android and iOS have their own malware too (booby-trapped apps, spyware, password stealers). No system is invulnerable."},
  "Une page web affiche « Votre PC est infecté, appelez ce numéro immédiatement ». C'est… ¦ Une alerte officielle de Windows": {"q":"A web page displays “Your PC is infected, call this number immediately”. This is…","e":"Microsoft never displays a number to call. You close the browser (using Task Manager if needed), you don't call, and you can report it on cybermalveillance.gouv.fr.","a":["An official Windows alert","A message from your antivirus","A tech support scam"]},
  "Un ver (worm) se distingue d'un virus parce qu'il… ¦ Se cache dans un logiciel d'apparence utile que tu installes toi-même": {"q":"A worm differs from a virus because it…","e":"WannaCry (2017) is the famous example: it exploited a flaw in SMB file sharing to jump from machine to machine. Hence the importance of updates.","a":["Hides in useful-looking software that you install yourself","Spreads on its own across the network, without any user action","Only runs in memory, never writing to disk"]},
  "Un « infostealer » est un malware qui… ¦ Vole les mots de passe, cookies et données enregistrées dans le navigateur": {"q":"An “infostealer” is malware that…","e":"Stolen credentials are resold in bulk. Session cookies even let attackers reuse a login already validated by MFA.","a":["Steals the passwords, cookies and data saved in the browser","Encrypts files and disks to demand a ransom","Hijacks the browser to display targeted ads"]},
  "Une attaque DDoS vise à… ¦ Intercepter le trafic entre un utilisateur et un serveur": {"q":"A DDoS attack aims to…","e":"Thousands of machines (often a botnet of hacked connected devices) flood the target. It is an attack on Availability, the A of the CIA triad.","a":["Intercept traffic between a user and a server","Take control of a server through an unpatched flaw","Make a service unavailable by overwhelming it with requests"]},
  "Quels signes peuvent indiquer qu'un poste est infecté ? ¦ Ralentissements et ventilateur à fond sans raison": {"q":"Which signs can indicate that a computer is infected?","e":"At the slightest doubt, you don't tinker alone: you disconnect the computer from the network and notify support.","a":["Slowdowns and the fan running at full speed for no reason","Files renamed with an unknown extension","A Windows update asking for a restart","Antivirus turned off by itself"]},
  "Pourquoi un infogéreur (MSP) est-il une cible de choix pour les attaquants ? ¦ Il utilise surtout des logiciels libres, réputés moins sûrs": {"q":"Why is a managed service provider (MSP) a prime target for attackers?","e":"Compromising an MSP means potentially reaching all of its customers. Hence MFA everywhere, least privilege (GDAP on the Microsoft side) and monitoring of remote access tools.","a":["It mostly uses open-source software, which is reputed to be less secure","Its remote admin access leads to many customers","It escapes the GDPR as a processor, so it is little monitored"]},
  "Un « zero-day », c'est… ¦ Une faille dont le correctif existe mais n'est pas installé": {"q":"A “zero-day” is…","e":"The vendor had “zero days” to fix it. A flaw that has already been fixed but not yet patched on your side is no longer a zero-day. Defense then relies on behavior detection (EDR), segmentation and published workarounds.","a":["A flaw for which a fix exists but is not installed","A flaw exploited before a fix is available","Malware that stays dormant until a specific date"]},
  "Le modèle « Ransomware-as-a-Service » (RaaS)… ¦ Est un exercice de simulation de rançongiciel vendu aux entreprises": {"q":"The “Ransomware-as-a-Service” (RaaS) model…","e":"Affiliates pay a share of the ransom to the developers. The result: many attacks, carried out by groups that do not need to be very technical.","a":["Is a ransomware simulation exercise sold to companies","Refers to a cloud-hosted ransomware that encrypts SharePoint and OneDrive data","Lets developers rent out their ransomware to “affiliates” who carry out the attacks"]},
  "La « double extorsion », c'est quand les attaquants… ¦ Chiffrent les données et menacent aussi de publier celles qu'ils ont volées": {"q":"“Double extortion” is when attackers…","e":"Having good backups is no longer enough: you also need to limit and detect data exfiltration (DLP, monitoring of outbound traffic, encryption).","a":["Encrypt the data and also threaten to publish what they have stolen","Encrypt the files twice, with two different keys","Encrypt the computers and then the backups, with a ransom for each"]},
  "Une attaque « supply chain » (chaîne d'approvisionnement)… ¦ Vise la logistique et les stocks d'une entreprise pour la paralyser": {"q":"A “supply chain” attack…","e":"SolarWinds (2020) or Kaseya (2021, via tools used by MSPs): a legitimate update served as a Trojan horse for thousands of organizations.","a":["Targets a company's logistics and inventory to paralyze it","Compromises a trusted supplier or software to reach its customers","Floods a supplier's website with fake orders to overload it"]},
  "Un malware « fileless » est difficile à détecter parce qu'il… ¦ Se déguise en fichier PDF ou image pour tromper l'utilisateur et l'antivirus": {"q":"“Fileless” malware is hard to detect because it…","e":"This is “living off the land”: the attacker uses the tools already present (PowerShell, WMI…). An antivirus that scans files sees nothing; you need an EDR that analyzes behavior. Polymorphic malware, by contrast, does leave a file on disk.","a":["Disguises itself as a PDF or image file to fool the user and the antivirus","Changes its signature with every infection (polymorphism) to evade antivirus","Runs in memory through legitimate tools (PowerShell…), with no file on disk"]},
  "Dans l'écosystème des ransomwares, un « initial access broker », c'est… ¦ Un criminel qui revend à d'autres groupes des accès déjà obtenus à des réseaux": {"q":"In the ransomware ecosystem, an “initial access broker” is…","e":"Crime is highly specialized: one steals access (VPN, RDP, accounts), another buys it to launch the encryption. Hence the importance of monitoring remote connections.","a":["A criminal who resells to other groups access already obtained to networks","An intermediary who negotiates the ransom amount with victims","An affiliate who deploys the encryption on behalf of a RaaS group"]},
  "Un « keylogger », c'est… ¦ Un bûcheron qui tient son journal de bord": {"q":"A “keylogger” is…","e":"It captures passwords, messages and card numbers to send them to the attacker. MFA limits the damage if a password is stolen this way.","a":["A lumberjack who keeps a logbook","A wireless keyboard that encrypts what you type","Software that records everything you type on the keyboard"]},
  "À quoi un botnet (réseau de machines piratées) sert-il typiquement ? ¦ Lancer des attaques DDoS": {"q":"What is a botnet (a network of hacked machines) typically used for?","e":"The “zombie” machines obey a command server. Their combined power is rented out or resold: DDoS, spam, mining, relays to mask other attacks.","a":["Launching DDoS attacks","Sending mass spam","Fixing the flaws of infected machines","Mining cryptocurrency at the victims' expense"]},
  "Un « wiper » est un malware qui… ¦ Chiffre les fichiers puis fournit la clé contre rançon": {"q":"A “wiper” is malware that…","e":"Its goal is destruction, often for sabotage. NotPetya (2017) posed as ransomware, but the data was unrecoverable: only offline backups can save the day.","a":["Encrypts files and then provides the key in exchange for a ransom","Erases or corrupts data with no real possibility of recovery","Cleans up the traces left by an antivirus"]},
  "Comment appelle-t-on (sigle) le serveur qui envoie les ordres aux machines infectées et reçoit leurs données ? ¦ C2": {"q":"What is the acronym for the server that sends orders to infected machines and receives their data?","e":"The command and control (C2) server remotely steers malware. Spotting and blocking its communications (domains, IPs, regular beacons) cuts the attacker off from their machines.","placeholder":"Acronym…","answers":["C2","C&C","CnC","C and C","Command and Control","Commande et controle","Serveur C2","c2","c&c","cnc","c and c","command and control","command & control","c2 server"]},
  "Avant de chiffrer, un ransomware lance « vssadmin delete shadows /all /quiet ». Quelle technique MITRE ATT&CK est-ce ? ¦ T1490 : Inhibit System Recovery": {"q":"Before encrypting, a ransomware runs “vssadmin delete shadows /all /quiet”. Which MITRE ATT&CK technique is this?","e":"Deleting shadow copies (VSS) prevents local restoration: this is T1490. The encryption itself falls under T1486. This command is an excellent detection signal for an EDR.","a":["T1490: Inhibit System Recovery","T1486: Data Encrypted for Impact","T1070: Indicator Removal"]},
  "Un « spyware » (logiciel espion), c'est un malware qui… ¦ chiffre tous tes fichiers pour réclamer une rançon": {"q":"A “spyware” is malware that…","e":"Spyware stays as discreet as possible in order to spy: sites visited, credentials, messages, sometimes the microphone or camera. Encrypting for a ransom is ransomware; spreading on its own is a worm.","a":["encrypts all your files to demand a ransom","quietly collects your information and sends it to a third party","displays pop-up ads in a loop","copies itself from one computer to another on its own"]},
  "Un « adware », c'est un logiciel qui… ¦ affiche des pubs intrusives, souvent installé avec un logiciel gratuit": {"q":"An “adware” is software that…","e":"Adware floods you with ads and changes the browser's home page or search engine. It often arrives as a “bonus” in the installer of free software downloaded from unofficial sites.","a":["displays intrusive ads, often installed with free software","automatically backs up your documents to a free cloud space","blocks ads and pop-ups on the sites you visit","updates your drivers in the background, without asking your opinion"]},
  "Quelle mesure permet le mieux de récupérer tes données après une attaque par rançongiciel ? ¦ Payer la rançon rapidement pour obtenir la clé": {"q":"Which measure best lets you recover your data after a ransomware attack?","e":"A disconnected (or immutable) backup is your real insurance: the ransomware cannot reach it. Paying guarantees neither recovery nor deletion of the stolen data, and the authorities advise against it.","a":["Quickly paying the ransom to get the key","Renaming the encrypted files with their old extension","Restoring from a recent backup kept offline","Restarting the PC in safe mode"]},
  "Avec un antivirus à jour, tu es protégé à 100 % contre tous les logiciels malveillants. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With an up-to-date antivirus, you are 100% protected against all malware.","e":"No tool stops everything: new malware, “zero-day” flaws and above all traps that make you act yourself (attachment, link, fake support) sometimes get through. Antivirus is one layer among others, along with updates, backups and your vigilance."},
  "Quels réflexes réduisent le risque d'infection de ton poste ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Installer les mises à jour dès qu'elles sont proposées": {"q":"Which habits reduce the risk of your computer being infected? (several answers)","e":"Updates fix the flaws that malware exploits, and an unexpected attachment may come from a hacked mailbox. Turning off the antivirus or using an admin account day to day, on the contrary, gives malware more power.","a":["Installing updates as soon as they are offered","Not opening an unexpected attachment, even from a known contact","Turning off the antivirus when it slows down the PC","Working day to day with an administrator account"]},
  "En cybersécurité, le sigle TTP désigne… ¦ les tactiques, techniques et procédures d'un attaquant": {"q":"In cybersecurity, the acronym TTP stands for…","e":"TTPs describe an attacker's behavior: their objective (tactic), how they achieve it (technique) and its concrete implementation (procedure). This is what MITRE ATT&CK catalogs.","a":["an attacker's tactics, techniques and procedures","technical penetration tests","the total time of propagation of a malware","persistent technical traces on a disk"]},
  "Pourquoi segmenter le réseau (VLAN, pare-feu internes) aide-t-il face aux malwares ? ¦ Cela accélère la détection des malwares par l'antivirus": {"q":"Why does segmenting the network (VLANs, internal firewalls) help against malware?","e":"A worm or ransomware that compromises one computer tries to pivot to other machines. Separate zones with filtered flows reduce this lateral movement and the scope affected.","a":["It speeds up malware detection by the antivirus","It limits the spread from an infected machine to the rest of the IS","It automatically encrypts traffic between computers","It removes the need for backups"]},
  "Pourquoi faut-il déployer vite les correctifs de sécurité, surtout sur les équipements exposés à Internet ? ¦ Parce que Windows coupe l'accès réseau des machines non corrigées": {"q":"Why should security patches be deployed quickly, especially on Internet-facing equipment?","e":"Publishing a patch also reveals the flaw: attackers analyze the patch and scan the Internet for unpatched systems. VPNs, firewalls and exposed servers are the first targets.","a":["Because Windows cuts off network access for unpatched machines","Because cumulative patches can no longer be installed after 30 days","Because published flaws are often exploited within a few days","Because a late patch disables the EDR's protection"]},
  "Un EDR se contente de comparer les fichiers à une base de signatures, exactement comme un antivirus classique. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An EDR just compares files against a signature database, exactly like a traditional antivirus.","e":"An EDR (Endpoint Detection and Response) continuously monitors the computer's behavior (processes, connections, changes), keeps telemetry for investigation and lets you respond remotely, for example by isolating the machine."},
  "Tu suspectes un rançongiciel sur un poste utilisateur. Remets les actions dans l'ordre : ¦ Déconnecter le poste du réseau sans l'éteindre": {"q":"You suspect ransomware on a user's computer. Put the actions in order:","e":"First isolate to stop the spread (without shutting down, to keep the memory), then alert. You preserve the evidence before analyzing, and you only restore once the threat is understood, otherwise you risk being reinfected.","items":["Disconnect the computer from the network without shutting it down","Alert support or the CISO","Preserve the traces for analysis","Identify the threat and the extent of the compromise","Restore from a clean backup"]},
  "Quel est le nom du CERT gouvernemental français, opéré par l'ANSSI, qui publie alertes et avis de sécurité ? ¦ CERT-FR": {"q":"What is the name of the French government CERT, operated by ANSSI, that publishes security alerts and advisories?","e":"CERT-FR (cert.ssi.gouv.fr) publishes alerts, vulnerability advisories and threat reports. For a victim who is an individual, a very small business or a local authority, first-level help goes through cybermalveillance.gouv.fr.","placeholder":"CERT name…","answers":["CERT-FR","CERTFR","CERT FR"]},
  "Le sigle APT (Advanced Persistent Threat) désigne… ¦ un malware grand public diffusé en masse par des campagnes d'e-mails": {"q":"The acronym APT (Advanced Persistent Threat) refers to…","e":"An APT is an organized, well-funded group, often state-linked, that targets specific victims and seeks to stay in the IS for a long time (espionage, sabotage). MITRE ATT&CK documents these groups and their techniques.","a":["mass-market malware spread by email campaigns","an organized, well-funded attacker who quietly maintains access over time","an unpatched flaw that has been present in the IS for several years","a new-generation antivirus that detects threats using AI"]},
  "Une équipe SOC utilise MITRE ATT&CK Navigator pour… ¦ scanner les vulnérabilités de ses serveurs exposés": {"q":"A SOC team uses MITRE ATT&CK Navigator to…","e":"Navigator color-codes the ATT&CK matrix: you mark the techniques covered by detections and those used by a group of interest, and so spot the blind spots to address first.","a":["scan its exposed servers for vulnerabilities","download malware samples sorted by group","map its detection coverage against ATT&CK techniques","automatically generate firewall rules"]},
  "En analyse de malware, un « dropper » ou « loader » est un programme dont le rôle principal est… ¦ de chiffrer les fichiers de la victime": {"q":"In malware analysis, a “dropper” or “loader” is a program whose main role is…","e":"It is the first stage of an infection: it installs itself quietly and then deploys the real payload (infostealer, remote access tool, ransomware). Detecting it early lets you break the chain before the impact.","a":["to encrypt the victim's files","to install or download another malicious payload onto the machine","to steal the passwords saved in the browser","to send spam from the infected machine"]},
  "Pourquoi recommande-t-on des sauvegardes hors ligne ou immuables contre les rançongiciels ? ¦ Parce que les attaquants détruisent d'abord les sauvegardes accessibles": {"q":"Why are offline or immutable backups recommended against ransomware?","e":"Ransomware operators prioritize targeting backup consoles and repositories to delete or encrypt them before launching the encryption, and prevent any restoration. A disconnected or write-locked (WORM) copy stays out of their reach.","a":["Because attackers first destroy the accessible backups","Because ransomware cannot encrypt backup files","Because immutable backups restore faster than others","Because ANSSI forbids connecting a backup to the production network"]},
  "Dans la matrice MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise, lesquelles sont des tactiques ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Persistence": {"q":"In the MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise matrix, which of these are tactics? (several answers)","e":"Persistence, Lateral Movement and Impact are tactics (attacker objectives). Obfuscation is a technique (T1027 “Obfuscated Files or Information”), that is, a means, not an objective.","a":["Persistence","Lateral Movement","Obfuscation","Impact"]},
  "Dans MITRE ATT&CK, la technique T1486 « Data Encrypted for Impact » (le chiffrement façon rançongiciel) est rattachée à la tactique Impact. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In MITRE ATT&CK, technique T1486 “Data Encrypted for Impact” (ransomware-style encryption) is attached to the Impact tactic.","e":"T1486 describes encrypting data to make it unavailable, the core of ransomware. It falls under the Impact tactic, along with, for example, T1490 “Inhibit System Recovery”."},
  "Quel outil à règles, créé chez VirusTotal, décrit des motifs (chaînes, octets, conditions) pour identifier et classer des échantillons de malware ? ¦ YARA": {"q":"Which rule-based tool, created at VirusTotal, describes patterns (strings, bytes, conditions) to identify and classify malware samples?","e":"A YARA rule combines text strings, hexadecimal sequences and conditions to recognize a malware family. It is used to scan files or memory and to share detection between teams.","placeholder":"Tool name…","answers":["YARA"]},
  "Dans MITRE ATT&CK, l'identifiant T1566 correspond à… ¦ Valid Accounts": {"q":"In MITRE ATT&CK, the identifier T1566 corresponds to…","e":"T1566 “Phishing” (Initial Access tactic) has as sub-techniques the attachment, the link, sending via a service and “voice phishing”. Valid Accounts is T1078, Exploit Public-Facing Application is T1190, External Remote Services is T1133.","a":["Valid Accounts","Phishing","Exploit Public-Facing Application","External Remote Services"]},
  "Pourquoi la technique T1078 « Valid Accounts » apparaît-elle sous plusieurs tactiques d'ATT&CK ? ¦ Parce qu'elle a été dupliquée par erreur dans plusieurs versions de la matrice": {"q":"Why does technique T1078 “Valid Accounts” appear under several ATT&CK tactics?","e":"A technique is attached to every tactic it serves. A stolen legitimate account lets you get in, stay in, gain more privileges and fly under the radar: T1078 therefore appears under Initial Access, Persistence and Privilege Escalation, among others.","a":["Because it was duplicated by mistake across several versions of the matrix","Because each tactic has its own copy with a different identifier","Because a single technique can serve several attacker objectives","Because it covers several platforms (Windows, cloud), each filed separately"]},
  "MITRE D3FEND est… ¦ une base des contre-mesures défensives, reliées aux techniques d'ATT&CK": {"q":"MITRE D3FEND is…","e":"D3FEND catalogs defensive techniques (hardening, detection, isolation, deception, eviction…) and links them to ATT&CK techniques. CISA's list of exploited vulnerabilities is the KEV catalog.","a":["a knowledge base of defensive countermeasures, linked to ATT&CK techniques","the former name of the ATT&CK matrix, before its 2018 overhaul","an open-source EDR published by MITRE and aligned with the ATT&CK matrix","the list of known exploited vulnerabilities published by CISA"]},
  "L'EDR remonte certutil.exe lancé par winword.exe avec l'option -urlcache vers une URL externe. Qu'est-ce qui rend cet événement suspect ? ¦ certutil.exe est un malware connu qui imite un binaire Windows": {"q":"The EDR reports certutil.exe launched by winword.exe with the -urlcache option to an external URL. What makes this event suspicious?","e":"certutil is a signed Microsoft tool, often hijacked to download or decode files (“living off the land”). Word launching this kind of tool is a typical lineage of a malicious macro: it is the sequence that raises the alert, not the binary alone. Blocking Office child processes requires an ASR rule; it is not the default behavior.","a":["certutil.exe is known malware that imitates a Windows binary","certutil.exe only exists on Windows Server, not on workstations","Windows prevents Word from creating child processes by default","A hijacked legitimate binary (LOLBin), with an abnormal parent-child relationship"]},
  "Sur un proxy, un poste contacte le même domaine toutes les 60 secondes, à quelques secondes près, avec des requêtes de taille quasi identique. Que suggère ce motif ? ¦ Une simple synchronisation de l'horloge système": {"q":"On a proxy, a computer contacts the same domain every 60 seconds, give or take a few seconds, with requests of almost identical size. What does this pattern suggest?","e":"An implant regularly polls its C2 to receive orders; the regularity, even with some randomness (jitter), is an indicator used in threat hunting. You then need to check the domain's reputation and age to rule out a legitimate service.","a":["A simple system clock synchronization","“Beaconing” to a command and control server","A Windows Update in progress","A port scan launched from the Internet"]},
  "Sur quoi Office s'appuie-t-il pour bloquer par défaut les macros VBA des fichiers téléchargés depuis Internet ? ¦ Sur la signature numérique du fichier, toujours absente des fichiers web": {"q":"What does Office rely on to block, by default, VBA macros in files downloaded from the Internet?","e":"Windows tags files that come from the Internet via the NTFS Zone.Identifier stream (ZoneId=3). Office uses it to block their macros; hence attackers' interest in containers that used to lose this mark, and defenders' interest in monitoring those formats.","a":["The file's digital signature, which is always missing from web files","The file extension, blocked if it ends with “m”","The “Mark of the Web”, stored in the Zone.Identifier alternate data stream","The file size, with macros blocked above a threshold"]},
  "Dans ATT&CK, une sous-technique s'identifie par l'ID de la technique suivi d'un point et de trois chiffres, par exemple T1059.001 pour PowerShell. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In ATT&CK, a sub-technique is identified by the technique ID followed by a dot and three digits, for example T1059.001 for PowerShell.","e":"T1059 is “Command and Scripting Interpreter” and T1059.001 is its PowerShell sub-technique. This format is used to write precise detections and reports, where the parent ID remains too broad."},
  "En investigation Windows, quels emplacements vérifies-tu en priorité pour repérer la persistance d'un malware ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les clés Run et RunOnce du registre": {"q":"In a Windows investigation, which locations do you check first to spot a malware's persistence? (several answers)","e":"Run/RunOnce keys (T1547.001), scheduled tasks (T1053.005) and services (T1543.003) are classic mechanisms for surviving a reboot. The ARP cache tells you about network neighbors, not about persistence.","a":["The Run and RunOnce registry keys","Scheduled tasks","Windows services","The ARP cache"]},
  "Déroulé typique d'une attaque par rançongiciel « opérée par des humains », selon les tactiques ATT&CK : remets les étapes dans l'ordre. ¦ Accès initial (Initial Access)": {"q":"Typical sequence of a “human-operated” ransomware attack, according to the ATT&CK tactics: put the steps in order.","e":"Attackers get in, steal privileged credentials, move to the key servers, exfiltrate data for double extortion, then encrypt last. Every step detected before Impact is a chance to stop the attack.","items":["Initial Access","Credential Access","Lateral Movement","Exfiltration","Impact (data encryption)"]},
  "Quel est l'identifiant de la tactique « Impact » dans MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise ? ¦ TA0040": {"q":"What is the identifier of the “Impact” tactic in MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise?","e":"Tactics carry a TA identifier: TA0001 for Initial Access, TA0040 for Impact. Impact groups the techniques for destroying, encrypting or manipulating data and systems.","placeholder":"TA00…","answers":["TA0040"]},
  "Un mot de passe solide, c'est… ¦ Une longue phrase, unique pour ce compte": {"q":"A strong password is…","e":"Length and uniqueness: a passphrase is hard to guess, and a hacked site does not compromise your other accounts. Replacing letters with symbols does not fool cracking tools.","a":["A long phrase, unique to this account","A common word with symbols (P@ssw0rd!)","A complicated word that you reuse everywhere"]},
  "Que veut dire MFA ? ¦ Accès fédéré Microsoft": {"q":"What does MFA stand for?","e":"MFA = one more proof on top of the password (app, code, key). Even if your password leaks, the hacker is blocked.","a":["Microsoft Federated Access","Multifactor authentication","Multi-device authorization"]},
  "Lesquels sont de vrais facteurs d'authentification ? ¦ Ce que tu sais (mot de passe)": {"q":"Which are genuine authentication factors?","e":"The three families: know, have, be. MFA combines at least two. Your email address is an identifier, not a proof.","a":["Something you know (password)","Something you have (phone, key)","Something you are (fingerprint, face)","Something you state (your email address)"]},
  "Pourquoi bloquer l'authentification héritée (POP, IMAP, SMTP basique) ? ¦ Elle n'apparaît pas dans les journaux Entra": {"q":"Why block legacy authentication (POP, IMAP, basic SMTP)?","e":"These protocols only accept a password: an attacker can bypass your MFA by going through them (password spray). Yet these sign-ins remain visible in the Entra logs (“Client app” filter).","a":["It doesn't appear in the Entra logs","It doesn't support MFA","It bypasses EOP's anti-spam filtering"]},
  "À quoi sert un gestionnaire de mots de passe ? ¦ À réutiliser ton mot de passe Windows sur tous tes sites": {"q":"What is a password manager for?","e":"You only remember a single master password (well protected, with MFA) and the tool manages all the others, which are different and complex.","a":["Reusing your Windows password on all your sites","Generating and remembering unique, strong passwords","Writing your passwords down on a digital sticky note"]},
  "Pourquoi les mots de passe sont-ils stockés sous forme « hachée » ? ¦ Pour les chiffrer avec une clé que seul l'admin détient": {"q":"Why are passwords stored in “hashed” form?","e":"Hashing is one-way: unlike encryption, no key can bring you back to the password. If the database leaks, the passwords are not directly readable.","a":["To encrypt them with a key that only the admin holds","So they aren't kept in plain text: fingerprints are compared instead","To speed up verification at sign-in"]},
  "Le principe du moindre privilège consiste à… ¦ Donner les mêmes droits à tous les membres d'une même équipe": {"q":"The principle of least privilege is about…","e":"The fewer rights an account has, the less damage an attacker can do if they compromise it.","a":["Giving the same rights to all members of the same team","Giving each person only the rights needed for their work","Removing an account's rights as soon as an alert concerns it"]},
  "Une attaque « pass-the-hash » permet de… ¦ S'authentifier avec l'empreinte d'un mot de passe, sans connaître le mot de passe": {"q":"A “pass-the-hash” attack makes it possible to…","e":"In a Windows environment, the NTLM hash stolen from memory is enough to authenticate elsewhere, without even cracking it. Replaying a Kerberos ticket is pass-the-ticket. Hence the importance of protecting privileged accounts and limiting their use.","a":["Authenticate with a password's hash, without knowing the password","Crack an NTLM hash offline to recover the password","Replay a stolen Kerberos ticket on another machine in the domain"]},
  "Le même mot de passe sur plusieurs sites : quel est le risque ? ¦ Tes comptes finissent par se disputer le même mot de passe": {"q":"Using the same password on several sites: what is the risk?","e":"This is “credential stuffing”: bots automatically try leaked credentials on hundreds of sites. A unique password per account breaks the chain.","a":["Your accounts end up fighting over the same password","If one site gets hacked, that password is tried everywhere else","It becomes easier to guess by brute force"]},
  "Quel site permet de vérifier si ton adresse mail apparaît dans une fuite de données connue ? ¦ VirusTotal de Google": {"q":"Which site lets you check whether your email address appears in a known data breach?","e":"haveibeenpwned.com lists public breaches (VirusTotal, for its part, analyzes files and links). If your address appears there, change the affected password (and everywhere you reused it), and enable MFA.","a":["Google's VirusTotal","Doctissimo, “virus” section","Have I Been Pwned"]},
  "Une clé de sécurité physique (FIDO2) ou une passkey résistent mieux au phishing qu'un code reçu par SMS. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A physical security key (FIDO2) or a passkey resists phishing better than a code received by SMS.","e":"True: they check the site's real address. On a fake site, they simply refuse to authenticate, whereas an SMS code can be copied by the hacker."},
  "La « fatigue MFA », c'est… ¦ Bombarder la victime de demandes MFA jusqu'à ce qu'elle accepte par lassitude": {"q":"“MFA fatigue” is…","e":"Countermeasure: number matching (entering the number shown on screen) in Microsoft Authenticator, and never approving a request you didn't trigger yourself.","a":["Bombarding the victim with MFA requests until they approve out of weariness","Pushing tired users to disable their own MFA","Hijacking SMS codes by cloning the victim's SIM card"]},
  "L'attaque par « password spraying » consiste à… ¦ Tester des millions de mots de passe sur un seul compte": {"q":"“Password spraying” is an attack that consists of…","e":"Few attempts per account, so no lockout. Replaying stolen credentials elsewhere is credential stuffing. Countermeasures: MFA, banned password list (Entra ID Password Protection) and monitoring of sign-in failures.","a":["Testing millions of passwords on a single account","Testing a few very common passwords on many accounts","Replaying stolen credentials on another site"]},
  "Le SSO (authentification unique) permet… ¦ De synchroniser les mots de passe AD vers le cloud": {"q":"SSO (single sign-on) allows you to…","e":"Fewer passwords to remember, and a central control point: disabling the account cuts access to all applications at once.","a":["Synchronize AD passwords to the cloud","Use the same password, typed into each application","Sign in once to access several applications"]},
  "Classe ces méthodes de MFA, de la moins sûre à la plus sûre : ¦ Code par SMS": {"q":"Rank these MFA methods, from least secure to most secure:","e":"Any MFA is better than none! But SMS can be intercepted (SIM swapping) and only FIDO2/passkey methods truly resist phishing.","items":["SMS code","Simple notification to approve","Notification with number matching","FIDO2 key or passkey"]},
  "Pourquoi séparer son compte administrateur de son compte de travail quotidien ? ¦ Pour que les actions d'admin ne soient pas tracées dans l'audit": {"q":"Why separate your administrator account from your daily work account?","e":"You read emails and browse with a standard account: a phishing email or malware opened there only gets limited rights. The admin account, protected by strong MFA, is only used for administration tasks.","a":["So that admin actions aren't tracked in the audit","So that malware opened day to day doesn't gain admin rights","So you can do without MFA on your daily work account"]},
  "Un compte de service (utilisé par une application) doit… ¦ Être membre des Admins du domaine pour éviter les erreurs d'accès": {"q":"A service account (used by an application) must…","e":"In Active Directory, managed service accounts (gMSA) change their password automatically. An overly powerful service account is an ideal target.","a":["Be a member of Domain Admins to avoid access errors","Be the personal account of the technician who installed the application","Have a long, unique password, minimal rights, and be monitored"]},
  "Microsoft et le NIST recommandent de forcer tous les utilisateurs à changer de mot de passe tous les 30 jours. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Microsoft and NIST recommend forcing all users to change their password every 30 days.","e":"False: forced changes that are too frequent lead to weak, predictable passwords (Summer2025!, Autumn2025!…). You change a password when a leak is suspected, and rely on length and MFA."},
  "Le « Kerberoasting » cible… ¦ Les comptes sans pré-authentification Kerberos, dont on casse la réponse AS-REP": {"q":"“Kerberoasting” targets…","e":"Any domain user can request these tickets. Targeting accounts without pre-authentication is AS-REP roasting; stealing the krbtgt key is the golden ticket. Countermeasure: very long passwords (or gMSA) for service accounts, and AES rather than RC4.","a":["Accounts without Kerberos pre-authentication, whose AS-REP response is cracked","AD service accounts, for which a ticket is requested to crack the password offline","The krbtgt account, whose key is stolen to forge TGTs"]},
  "Un « golden ticket » Kerberos, c'est… ¦ Un faux ticket forgé avec la clé du compte krbtgt, qui donne un accès quasi illimité au domaine": {"q":"A Kerberos “golden ticket” is…","e":"It assumes the attacker has already compromised a domain controller. To invalidate it, you reset the krbtgt account's password twice.","a":["A fake ticket forged with the krbtgt account's key, giving almost unlimited access to the domain","A service ticket forged with a service account's hash, limited to that service","A TGT stolen from memory and then replayed on another machine (pass-the-ticket)"]},
  "Quel compte Active Directory, s'il est compromis, permet de forger des « golden tickets » Kerberos ? ¦ krbtgt": {"q":"Which Active Directory account, if compromised, makes it possible to forge Kerberos “golden tickets”?","e":"Its key signs all the domain's Kerberos tickets. If it is compromised, you reset its password twice.","placeholder":"Account name","answers":["krbtgt"]},
  "Une longue phrase de passe (quatre mots au hasard, par exemple) peut être plus solide qu'un mot de passe court plein de symboles. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A long passphrase (four random words, for example) can be stronger than a short password full of symbols.","e":"True: length matters more than complexity in resisting cracking. And a phrase is easier to remember without writing it on a sticky note."},
  "Ton téléphone affiche une demande de validation MFA alors que tu ne te connectes à rien. Tu… ¦ Refuses et préviens le support : ton mot de passe a fuité": {"q":"Your phone shows an MFA approval request even though you aren't signing in to anything. You…","e":"An unsolicited MFA request means your password has been entered by someone else. Deny it, report it, then change your password.","a":["Deny it and notify support: your password has leaked","Approve it: it's probably an app reconnecting on its own","Ignore the request, it will expire by itself after a minute"]},
  "Une passkey, c'est… ¦ Un mot de passe complexe généré et stocké par le navigateur": {"q":"A passkey is…","e":"The private key never leaves the device and only works for the genuine site: nothing to steal, nothing to type into a fake page. It is a phishing-resistant FIDO2 method. The code that changes every 30 seconds is a TOTP.","a":["A complex password generated and stored by the browser","A six-digit code generated every 30 seconds by an app","A key pair tied to the site, unlocked by biometrics or PIN"]},
  "Quel protocole d'authentification Windows, plus ancien que Kerberos, est exposé au pass-the-hash et aux attaques par relais ? ¦ NTLM": {"q":"Which Windows authentication protocol, older than Kerberos, is exposed to pass-the-hash and relay attacks?","e":"NTLM authenticates with a hash of the password, which can be reused as is. Microsoft is deprecating it: you audit its use then restrict it, and enable SMB and LDAP signing against relay.","placeholder":"Acronym…","answers":["NTLM","NTLMv1","NTLMv2","NT LAN Manager"]},
  "Sur un contrôleur de domaine, quel signal oriente vers du Kerberoasting ? ¦ Des événements 4625 (échec d'ouverture de session) en rafale sur krbtgt": {"q":"On a domain controller, which signal points to Kerberoasting?","e":"The attacker requests service tickets (4769) to crack offline the passwords of accounts with an SPN, preferring RC4, which is easier to crack. A series of 4771 events rather suggests password spraying. Countermeasures: enforce AES, long passwords or gMSA, and “decoy” accounts with an SPN.","a":["A burst of 4625 events (logon failure) on krbtgt","A series of 4769 events, in RC4 (0x17), across several service accounts","A series of 4771 events (pre-authentication failure) on several accounts"]},
  "Tu consultes ta messagerie sur un ordinateur en libre-service (médiathèque, hôtel). Au moment de te connecter, le site propose « Rester connecté ». Tu… ¦ acceptes, pour gagner du temps la prochaine fois": {"q":"You check your email on a public-use computer (library, hotel). When you sign in, the site offers “Stay signed in”. You…","e":"On a shared computer, a session left open lets the next person access your account without a password or MFA. You decline “Stay signed in”, sign out and close the browser.","a":["accept, to save time next time","decline, then sign out and close the browser when you finish","accept, but turn off the screen when you leave","decline, but leave the tab open for the next visit"]},
  "Avec un gestionnaire de mots de passe, le mot de passe maître est le seul que tu dois vraiment retenir. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With a password manager, the master password is the only one you really have to remember.","e":"The manager generates and remembers unique passwords for each site; you only memorize the master password. It must therefore be long, unique, and protected by MFA if the manager allows it."},
  "Un collègue te demande ton mot de passe pour avancer sur un dossier pendant tes congés. Tu… ¦ le lui donnes, c'est un collègue de confiance": {"q":"A colleague asks for your password so they can move a file forward while you're on leave. You…","e":"A password is personal: everything done with your account is attributed to you. The right reflex is to give access to the resource (sharing, delegation), never your identity.","a":["give it to them, they're a trusted colleague","decline and share the file with them (or ask for a delegation)","write it on a sticky note for them and change it when you're back","send it to them on Teams and then delete the message"]},
  "Quelles informations faut-il éviter dans un mot de passe ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le prénom de ton enfant ou de ton animal": {"q":"What information should you avoid in a password? (several answers)","e":"Personal information is often found on social media and is tried first by attackers. Random words unrelated to you are far safer.","a":["Your child's or pet's name","Your date of birth","A string of randomly chosen words","The name of your favorite football team"]},
  "Comment appelle-t-on l'attaque qui consiste à essayer toutes les combinaisons possibles jusqu'à trouver le mot de passe ? ¦ force brute": {"q":"What is the name of the attack that consists of trying every possible combination until the password is found?","e":"A brute-force attack methodically tries every combination. The longer the password, the more the number of combinations explodes and the more unrealistic the attack becomes.","placeholder":"Name of the attack","answers":["force brute","brute force","bruteforce","brute-force","attaque par force brute","attaque en force brute","attaque brute force","attaque par brute force","brute force attack","brute-force attack"]},
  "Le « credential stuffing », c'est… ¦ deviner le mot de passe d'une personne à partir de ses réseaux sociaux": {"q":"“Credential stuffing” is…","e":"Credential stuffing exploits password reuse: credentials stolen from one site are automatically replayed elsewhere. Trying a common password on many accounts is password spraying.","a":["guessing a person's password from their social media","trying a common password on thousands of accounts","testing username/password pairs from breaches on other sites","intercepting a password on public Wi-Fi"]},
  "Pourquoi Microsoft Authenticator demande-t-il désormais de saisir un nombre affiché à l'écran de connexion (number matching) ? ¦ Pour vérifier que l'appli Authenticator du téléphone est bien à jour": {"q":"Why does Microsoft Authenticator now ask you to enter a number shown on the sign-in screen (number matching)?","e":"With a simple “Approve” notification, a harassed user sometimes ends up accepting an attacker's request. Number matching forces you to type the number displayed on the sign-in screen, which only the person actually signing in can see.","a":["To check that the Authenticator app on the phone is up to date","To replace the password with a one-time code","To encrypt the communication between the phone and the PC","To counter MFA fatigue: you have to see the sign-in screen to approve"]},
  "Le « salage » (salt) d'un mot de passe fait que deux utilisateurs ayant le même mot de passe n'obtiennent pas le même hash. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"“Salting” a password means two users with the same password do not get the same hash.","e":"The salt is a random value specific to each account, added before hashing. It makes hashes different for the same password and prevents the use of precomputed tables (rainbow tables)."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes d'une connexion avec une passkey : ¦ Tu choisis « Se connecter avec une passkey »": {"q":"Put the steps of a passkey sign-in in order:","e":"The private key never leaves your device: it signs a unique challenge that the site verifies with the public key registered when the passkey was created. There is therefore no reusable secret to steal.","items":["You choose “Sign in with a passkey”","The site sends a random challenge","You unlock your device (fingerprint, face or PIN)","The device signs the challenge with the private key","The site verifies the signature with the registered public key"]},
  "Un attaquant vole le cookie de session d'un utilisateur déjà connecté. Que peut-il faire ? ¦ Utiliser la session sans connaître le mot de passe ni repasser la MFA": {"q":"An attacker steals the session cookie of a user who is already signed in. What can they do?","e":"The cookie proves that an authentication (MFA included) has already taken place: replaying it is enough as long as the session is valid. Hence the value of short sessions, continuous access evaluation and phishing-resistant methods.","a":["Use the session without knowing the password or going through MFA again","Nothing, the cookie is useless without the password","Only read the user's name","Only reset the victim's password"]},
  "Un kit de phishing « adversary-in-the-middle » (type Evilginx) relaie la vraie page de connexion. Quelle méthode MFA lui résiste ? ¦ Notification push avec number matching": {"q":"An “adversary-in-the-middle” phishing kit (Evilginx type) relays the real sign-in page. Which MFA method resists it?","e":"FIDO2 ties the signature to the site's real domain (origin): on a fake domain, the key refuses to respond or its response is unusable. Codes and notifications are simply relayed by the proxy, which then captures the session cookie.","a":["Push notification with number matching","FIDO2 security key or passkey","Code received by SMS","One-time code (TOTP) from an app"]},
  "Que recommande le NIST (SP 800-63B) pour les mots de passe choisis par les utilisateurs ? ¦ Imposer au moins une majuscule, un chiffre et un symbole": {"q":"What does NIST (SP 800-63B) recommend for passwords chosen by users?","e":"NIST calls for rejecting passwords found in breaches or common lists, and discourages arbitrary composition rules. It recommends instead allowing paste (for password managers) and prohibits hints.","a":["Require at least one uppercase letter, one digit and one symbol","Forbid copy-paste in the password field","Compare them against a list of compromised or overly common passwords","Offer a password hint in case of forgetting"]},
  "Dans Active Directory, les membres du groupe « Protected Users » ne peuvent plus s'authentifier en NTLM. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Active Directory, members of the “Protected Users” group can no longer authenticate with NTLM.","e":"Protected Users hardens sensitive accounts: no NTLM, no DES or RC4 for Kerberos, no delegation, and short-lived TGTs. Test before putting service accounts in it, as they may break."},
  "Quelles mesures réduisent le risque de vol d'identifiants en mémoire sur un poste Windows ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Activer Credential Guard": {"q":"Which measures reduce the risk of credential theft from memory on a Windows workstation? (several answers)","e":"Credential Guard isolates secrets in a virtualized environment and RunAsPPL protects the LSASS process. Enabling WDigest does the opposite, causing reversible passwords to be stored in memory, a gift for Mimikatz.","a":["Enable Credential Guard","Enable LSA protection (RunAsPPL)","Enable WDigest (UseLogonCredential = 1)","Add sensitive accounts to the Protected Users group"]},
  "Quelle solution Microsoft attribue et renouvelle automatiquement un mot de passe unique pour le compte administrateur local de chaque poste ? ¦ LAPS": {"q":"Which Microsoft solution automatically assigns and rotates a unique password for the local administrator account of each workstation?","e":"LAPS (now built into Windows as Windows LAPS) prevents a single local admin password across the whole fleet from allowing lateral movement from machine to machine. The password is stored in AD or Entra ID with restricted read rights.","placeholder":"Name of the solution","answers":["LAPS","Windows LAPS","Local Administrator Password Solution"]},
  "Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management (PIM) sert à… ¦ remplacer la MFA par une approbation pour les comptes à privilèges": {"q":"Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management (PIM) is used to…","e":"PIM applies least privilege over time (just-in-time): the admin is “eligible” and only activates their role for a limited duration, with MFA, justification or approval. Activations are logged.","a":["replace MFA with an approval for privileged accounts","automatically disable accounts inactive for 90 days","encrypt and rotate administrators' passwords","activate an admin role temporarily, on request and with justification"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les échanges Kerberos pour accéder à un service : ¦ AS-REQ : le client s'authentifie auprès du KDC": {"q":"Put the Kerberos exchanges for accessing a service in order:","e":"The TGT acts as a “badge” with the KDC to obtain service tickets, which are then presented to the target server. The user's password only comes into play in the initial exchange (AS-REQ / AS-REP): after that, everything relies on tickets.","items":["AS-REQ: the client authenticates to the KDC","AS-REP: the KDC issues a TGT","TGS-REQ: the client presents its TGT and requests a service ticket","TGS-REP: the KDC issues the service ticket","AP-REQ: the client presents the service ticket to the server"]},
  "Le modèle d'administration en tiers (tiering) dans Active Directory consiste à… ¦ séparer les comptes admin par niveau (AD, serveurs, postes) et les cloisonner": {"q":"The tiered administration model (tiering) in Active Directory consists of…","e":"Tier 0: AD and whatever controls it, tier 1: servers, tier 2: workstations; an account from one tier never signs in to a lower tier. If a domain admin signs in to a compromised workstation, their credentials can be stolen there: tiering ensures a user workstation never sees tier 0 credentials.","a":["separating admin accounts by level (AD, servers, workstations) and isolating them from each other","giving admins three password levels depending on their seniority","distributing accounts by department into separate OUs with their GPOs","placing domain controllers on three sites for redundancy"]},
  "Sur quel port le service Kerberos (KDC) écoute-t-il par défaut ? ¦ 389": {"q":"Which port does the Kerberos service (KDC) listen on by default?","e":"Kerberos uses port 88 (TCP and UDP). 389 and 636 correspond to LDAP and LDAPS, 445 to SMB.","a":["389","88","445","636"]},
  "L'attaque « AS-REP roasting » cible… ¦ le compte krbtgt, dont la clé chiffre les TGT du domaine": {"q":"The “AS-REP roasting” attack targets…","e":"Without pre-authentication, anyone can request an AS-REP for the account and obtain a portion encrypted with its key, to be cracked offline. Targeting accounts with an SPN is Kerberoasting.","a":["the krbtgt account, whose key encrypts the domain's TGTs","service accounts with an SPN (TGS tickets)","accounts with Kerberos pre-authentication disabled","computer accounts whose password has never been changed"]},
  "Une attaque DCSync repose sur… ¦ un accès physique ou console à un contrôleur de domaine": {"q":"A DCSync attack relies on…","e":"DCSync abuses the replication protocol (MS-DRSR): an account with the “Replicating Directory Changes” and “… All” rights can retrieve the hashes, including krbtgt's, without touching the DC's disk. Copying NTDS.dit is another technique.","a":["physical or console access to a domain controller","copying the NTDS.dit file via a shadow copy (VSS)","exploiting a flaw in a domain controller's DNS service","replication rights to obtain the hashes by impersonating a DC"]},
  "En quoi un « silver ticket » diffère-t-il d'un golden ticket ? ¦ Il est forgé avec le hash d'un compte de service et ne vaut que pour ce service": {"q":"How does a “silver ticket” differ from a golden ticket?","e":"The silver ticket is a service ticket forged with the service account's key: its scope is limited to that service, but there is no exchange with the DC, so fewer traces on the KDC side. The golden ticket, for its part, is a TGT forged with the krbtgt key.","a":["It is forged with a service account's hash and is only valid for that service","It is forged with the krbtgt hash but has a shorter lifetime","It requires a certificate from the enterprise certification authority","It relies on NTLM and only works on old domains"]},
  "Réinitialiser une seule fois le mot de passe du compte krbtgt suffit à invalider tous les golden tickets existants. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Resetting the krbtgt account's password just once is enough to invalidate all existing golden tickets.","e":"The DC also keeps krbtgt's previous password to validate tickets in use: you must reset it twice, letting replication happen between the two, to invalidate forged tickets."},
  "Quelles mesures rendent le Kerberoasting beaucoup plus difficile ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Utiliser des gMSA pour les comptes de service": {"q":"Which measures make Kerberoasting much harder? (several answers)","e":"Kerberoasting cracks offline a ticket encrypted with the service account's key: a long, random password (native with gMSAs) and abandoning RC4 make cracking unrealistic. SMB signing protects against NTLM relay, not against this attack.","a":["Use gMSAs for service accounts","Enforce very long, random passwords on service accounts with an SPN","Disable RC4 and enforce AES for Kerberos","Enable SMB signing on workstations"]},
  "Quel mécanisme, activé sur LDAPS, lie l'authentification à la session TLS pour empêcher le relais NTLM ? ¦ channel binding": {"q":"Which mechanism, enabled on LDAPS, binds authentication to the TLS session to prevent NTLM relay?","e":"Channel binding (EPA) includes a fingerprint of the TLS channel in the authentication: an attacker relaying the exchange from another TLS session is rejected. It is combined with LDAP signing for unencrypted connections.","placeholder":"Name of the mechanism","answers":["channel binding","LDAP channel binding","channel binding token","channel binding tokens","CBT","liaison de canal","liaison de canaux","liaison de canal LDAP","EPA","Extended Protection for Authentication","protection étendue de l'authentification","protection étendue","ldap channel binding","cbt","epa","extended protection for authentication"]},
  "L'attaque « Shadow Credentials » consiste à… ¦ cloner la carte à puce d'un administrateur pour ouvrir sa session": {"q":"The “Shadow Credentials” attack consists of…","e":"With write access to this attribute (used by Windows Hello for Business), the attacker registers their own key and obtains a TGT for the targeted account through certificate-based authentication (PKINIT). Monitoring changes to msDS-KeyCredentialLink is therefore essential.","a":["cloning an administrator's smart card to open their session","adding a key to an account's msDS-KeyCredentialLink to authenticate as it","creating a hidden account whose ACLs conceal its presence in the directory","copying the passwords saved in an admin's browser"]},
  "La règle de sauvegarde 3-2-1, c'est… ¦ 3 sauvegardes par jour, conservées 2 semaines, dont 1 testée": {"q":"The 3-2-1 backup rule is…","e":"3 copies of the data, 2 types of media, 1 copy off-site (or even offline) to survive a fire or a ransomware attack.","a":["3 backups per day, kept for 2 weeks, 1 of them tested","3 copies, on 2 different media, 1 of them off-site","3 copies on the same NAS, in 2 formats, 1 of them encrypted"]},
  "Les grandes phases de réponse à un incident, dans l'ordre : ¦ Préparation": {"q":"The main phases of incident response, in order:","e":"This is the classic cycle (inspired by NIST): you prepare, you detect, you contain then clean up and restore, and finally you learn the lessons.","items":["Preparation","Detection and analysis","Containment, eradication and recovery","Lessons learned"]},
  "Compte compromis : mot de passe réinitialisé. Il faut aussi… ¦ Révoquer les sessions et jetons actifs": {"q":"Compromised account: password reset. You must also…","e":"The access token lasts about an hour, but the refresh token can remain valid much longer: without revocation, the attacker keeps access despite the new password.","a":["Revoke active sessions and tokens","Wait for the tokens to expire on their own (1 h)","Reset the password again within 24 h"]},
  "Une sauvegarde branchée en permanence au réseau est à l'abri d'un ransomware. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A backup permanently connected to the network is safe from ransomware.","e":"False: if the ransomware can reach it, it encrypts it too. You need at least one offline or immutable (unmodifiable) copy."},
  "Quelles mesures limitent l'impact d'un ransomware ? ¦ Des sauvegardes hors ligne testées régulièrement": {"q":"Which measures limit the impact of ransomware?","e":"Tested backups, patches, least privilege and segmentation reduce the impact. A NAS mounted as a network drive, on the other hand, gets encrypted along with everything else: the backup must be offline or immutable.","a":["Offline backups that are regularly tested","Up-to-date workstations and servers","Limited rights for users","Backups on a NAS mounted as a network drive"]},
  "Tu as cliqué sur un lien douteux et saisi ton mot de passe. Premier réflexe ? ¦ Changer ton mot de passe sans en parler à personne": {"q":"You clicked a suspicious link and entered your password. What is your first reflex?","e":"Every minute counts: the password can be reset and sessions cut before the attacker uses them. Reporting a mistake makes you a hero, not a culprit.","a":["Change your password without telling anyone","Notify support or the security team right away","Unplug the internet box for the whole company"]},
  "Une demande de rançon s'affiche sur ton PC. Tu… ¦ Éteins le PC d'un appui long, puis préviens le support": {"q":"A ransom demand appears on your PC. You…","e":"Isolating prevents spread to other machines; not shutting down preserves useful traces in memory. Trying to clean up yourself destroys evidence: leave it to the response team.","a":["Turn off the PC with a long press, then notify support","Reboot in safe mode to remove the virus","Cut the network without turning off the PC, and notify support"]},
  "Payer la rançon garantit de récupérer ses données. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Paying the ransom guarantees you will get your data back.","e":"False: there is no guarantee, and you fund the criminals (who may come back). The French authorities advise against paying."},
  "En France, quel service public aide les victimes de cybermalveillance (particuliers, entreprises, collectivités) ? ¦ cybermalveillance.gouv.fr": {"q":"In France, which public service helps victims of cybermalveillance (individuals, businesses, local authorities)?","e":"Online diagnosis, advice and referral to service providers. 17Cyber can also provide help. PHAROS is used to report illegal content, and CERT-FR mainly handles incidents affecting government bodies and critical operators.","a":["cybermalveillance.gouv.fr","pharos.interieur.gouv.fr","cert.ssi.gouv.fr"]},
  "Pourquoi éviter d'éteindre brutalement un poste compromis ? ¦ L'arrêt brutal efface les journaux d'événements du disque": {"q":"Why avoid abruptly shutting down a compromised workstation?","e":"Running processes, network connections, sometimes encryption keys: all of this lives in RAM. The logs, for their part, remain on the disk. You isolate from the network, then the experts decide what comes next.","a":["An abrupt shutdown erases the event logs from the disk","RAM holds traces useful to the investigation that would disappear","Windows then locks the signed-in user's account"]},
  "Un « playbook » de réponse à incident, c'est… ¦ Le registre où l'on consigne chaque action pendant l'incident": {"q":"An incident response “playbook” is…","e":"Phishing, compromised account, ransomware… In the middle of a crisis, you don't improvise: you follow the playbook, which you have tested beforehand. The register of actions is the log (main courante); the final report is the RETEX (lessons-learned review).","a":["The register in which every action is recorded during the incident","The report written after the incident to learn lessons","A procedure written in advance for a given type of incident"]},
  "Pendant un incident, que faut-il consigner ? ¦ L'heure de chaque constat et de chaque action": {"q":"During an incident, what should be recorded?","e":"A precise log helps the investigation, the insurer, the filing of a complaint and the lessons-learned review. You never write passwords in it: this document gets circulated.","a":["The time of each finding and each action","Who did what","The passwords of the affected accounts","The affected machines and accounts"]},
  "Le retour d'expérience (RETEX) après un incident sert à… ¦ Comprendre ce qui s'est passé pour améliorer défenses et procédures": {"q":"The post-incident review (RETEX) is used to…","e":"What worked? What was missing? The decided actions are followed through to the end, otherwise the same incident will come back.","a":["Understand what happened to improve defenses and procedures","Identify who is to blame for the mistake that allowed the attack","Draft the complaint to be sent to investigators"]},
  "Plan de continuité (PCA) et plan de reprise (PRA) : ¦ Le PRA maintient l'activité pendant la crise ; le PCA organise le redémarrage après un sinistre": {"q":"Business continuity plan (PCA) and disaster recovery plan (PRA):","e":"The PCA plans degraded modes (paper-based work, backup site…); the PRA describes how to restore systems, in order and within deadlines (RTO, RPO).","a":["The PRA keeps the business running during the crisis; the PCA organizes the restart after a disaster","The PCA keeps the business running during the crisis; the PRA organizes the restart after a disaster","The PCA covers premises and staff; the PRA only concerns workstations"]},
  "Une sauvegarde « immuable »… ¦ Est chiffrée avec une clé que seul l'administrateur de sauvegarde connaît": {"q":"An “immutable” backup…","e":"If the attacker steals an admin account, they cannot erase these backups. It is a major countermeasure against ransomware, in addition to offline copies (which are disconnected but not necessarily locked).","a":["Is encrypted with a key that only the backup administrator knows","Is stored offline, on a tape disconnected from the production network","Cannot be modified or deleted during its retention period, even by an admin"]},
  "Réponse à un ransomware, dans l'ordre : ¦ Isoler les machines touchées du réseau": {"q":"Ransomware response, in order:","e":"Restoring before closing the entry door means getting reinfected. Also remember the CNIL within 72 h if personal data is affected.","items":["Isolate the affected machines from the network","Notify the crisis team and the competent authorities","Identify the entry point and the extent of the attack","Eradicate: clean up, fix the flaw, change the secrets","Restore from clean backups","Conduct the lessons-learned review"]},
  "Pourquoi porter plainte après une cyberattaque ? ¦ C'est souvent exigé par l'assureur, et ça permet l'enquête": {"q":"Why file a complaint after a cyberattack?","e":"The complaint opens legal proceedings, helps dismantle criminal groups and is often a condition for compensation by cyber insurance.","a":["It is often required by the insurer, and it enables an investigation","It is mandatory to notify the breach to the CNIL","It triggers free on-site intervention by the ANSSI"]},
  "En analyse forensique, la « chaîne de possession » garantit… ¦ Que l'image disque a été faite avec un bloqueur d'écriture": {"q":"In forensic analysis, the “chain of custody” guarantees…","e":"You work on a copy (image) computed with a fingerprint (hash), and every transfer of the evidence is tracked: if the hash changes or a link is missing, the evidence is no longer reliable before a judge. The write blocker protects the original during copying, but tracks nothing.","a":["That the disk image was made with a write blocker","That the evidence is intact and it is known who handled it, and when","That the attack chain was traced back to its author"]},
  "Comment appelle-t-on, en français, l'analyse menée après un incident pour en tirer des leçons (sigle) ? ¦ RETEX": {"q":"What is the French acronym for the analysis carried out after an incident to learn lessons from it?","e":"The lessons-learned review is done without looking for someone to blame: what worked, what was missing, what actions to take going forward?","placeholder":"Acronym","answers":["RETEX","REX","Retour d'expérience","lessons learned","post-incident review","after-action review","aar","pir"]},
  "Tu as cliqué sur un lien de phishing sans rien saisir : il suffit de supprimer le mail, inutile de prévenir le support. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You clicked a phishing link without entering anything: just delete the email, no need to notify support.","e":"False: a simple click can trigger a download or reveal that your address is active. Reporting quickly allows the workstation to be checked and the link to be blocked for colleagues."},
  "Quelles actions relèvent du confinement d'un incident ? ¦ Isoler le poste infecté du réseau via l'EDR": {"q":"Which actions are part of incident containment?","e":"Containing means preventing spread as quickly as possible, before eradicating and restoring. The lessons-learned review comes at the very end.","a":["Isolating the infected workstation from the network via the EDR","Writing the lessons-learned review","Disabling the compromised account","Blocking the attacker's server address on the firewall"]},
  "Pourquoi calcule-t-on l'empreinte SHA-256 d'une image disque saisie lors d'une enquête ? ¦ Pour compresser l'image et gagner de la place": {"q":"Why compute the SHA-256 hash of a disk image seized during an investigation?","e":"The same hash recomputed at any time proves the integrity of the evidence. You analyze a copy, never the original, and every handling is tracked.","a":["To compress the image and save space","To prove later that the copy has not been modified","To encrypt the image and protect it from theft"]},
  "Pendant une crise cyber, pourquoi prévoir un canal de communication « hors bande » ? ¦ Parce que la messagerie interne peut être coupée ou lue par l'attaquant": {"q":"During a cyber crisis, why plan an “out-of-band” communication channel?","e":"If the attacker controls Active Directory or the email system, they follow the response live. You prepare in advance phones, a separate messaging system and a paper contact list.","a":["Because internal email may be cut off or read by the attacker","To avoid saturating the bandwidth already used by the investigation","Because the insurer requires it to cover the loss"]},
  "Collecte de preuves : l'ordre de volatilité (RFC 3227), de la donnée la plus éphémère à la plus durable. ¦ Registres et cache du processeur": {"q":"Evidence collection: the order of volatility (RFC 3227), from the most ephemeral data to the most durable.","e":"You first capture what disappears at shutdown: RAM contains processes, keys and active connections. Hence the rule: isolate from the network without shutting down, then take a memory dump.","items":["CPU registers and cache","RAM (processes, network connections, ARP table)","Temporary files and swap file","Hard disk","Backups and archives"]},
  "Ton antivirus signale un fichier malveillant sur ton poste de travail. Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu ignores l'alerte : l'antivirus l'a sans doute déjà bloqué": {"q":"Your antivirus flags a malicious file on your workstation. What do you do?","e":"An antivirus alert must always be escalated: support checks whether the threat was actually blocked or whether other workstations are affected. Deleting the file yourself erases traces, and forwarding it would spread the threat.","a":["You ignore the alert: the antivirus has probably already blocked it","You notify support or the security team following the internal procedure","You delete the file yourself and empty the recycle bin","You send the file to a colleague for their opinion"]},
  "En cybersécurité, un « incident de sécurité », c'est… ¦ Une demande d'installation de logiciel adressée au support informatique": {"q":"In cybersecurity, a “security incident” is…","e":"A security incident harms (or threatens to harm) confidentiality, integrity or availability: hacked account, data leak, ransomware… A simple support request is not one.","a":["A software installation request sent to IT support","A forgotten password reported by a user to support","An event that threatens confidentiality, integrity or availability","A Windows update that takes longer than expected"]},
  "Si tu penses avoir provoqué un incident (par exemple en ouvrant une pièce jointe piégée), il vaut mieux le signaler tout de suite, même si tu crains d'être blâmé. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"If you think you caused an incident (for example by opening a booby-trapped attachment), it is better to report it right away, even if you fear being blamed.","e":"Every minute counts: a quick report helps limit the spread. Security teams a thousand times prefer an honest alert to a hidden incident."},
  "Tu trouves un fichier suspect sur ton PC. Pourquoi ne pas le supprimer toi-même avant de prévenir le support ? ¦ Il peut servir de preuve pour comprendre ce qui s'est passé": {"q":"You find a suspicious file on your PC. Why not delete it yourself before notifying support?","e":"The suspicious file is a valuable clue: it helps the security team identify the threat, its origin and any other machines affected. Deleting it erases useful traces.","a":["It can serve as evidence to understand what happened","Windows would automatically restore it on restart","The antivirus will delete it anyway at the next scan","Only support is allowed to empty the recycle bin"]},
  "Quels signes peuvent indiquer que ton compte a été piraté ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Des mails envoyés depuis ta boîte que tu n'as pas écrits": {"q":"Which signs may indicate that your account has been hacked? (several answers)","e":"Unknown emails in “Sent Items”, exotic sign-ins and surprise MFA requests are classic signs of compromise. A meeting reminder is normal behavior.","a":["Emails sent from your mailbox that you didn't write","A sign-in alert from a country where you are not","An automatic meeting reminder in Teams","MFA approval requests that you didn't trigger"]},
  "En réponse à incident, comment appelle-t-on l'étape qui consiste à isoler la menace pour l'empêcher de se propager ? ¦ confinement": {"q":"In incident response, what is the name of the step that consists of isolating the threat to stop it from spreading?","e":"Containment (or isolation) limits the damage: isolating a workstation from the network, blocking an account, cutting a flow. You then remove the threat (eradication) before restoring.","placeholder":"One word…","answers":["confinement","endiguement","containment","isolement","isolation","isolating","containing"]},
  "Lors d'une cyberattaque importante, l'entreprise réunit une « cellule de crise ». Quel est son rôle ? ¦ Réparer elle-même les postes et serveurs infectés": {"q":"During a major cyberattack, the company convenes a “crisis team”. What is its role?","e":"The crisis team brings together management, IT, security, legal and communications to make decisions, prioritize actions and inform employees, customers and authorities. The technical teams, for their part, carry out the investigation and remediation.","a":["Repair the infected workstations and servers itself","Steer the response: decide, coordinate and manage communication","Replace the IT department for the whole crisis","Carry out the technical analysis of the compromised machines"]},
  "Pendant une cyberattaque, tu peux sans risque discuter de la situation par la messagerie de l'entreprise, même si elle est peut-être compromise. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"During a cyberattack, you can safely discuss the situation through the company's email system, even if it may be compromised.","e":"If email is compromised, the attacker can read the exchanges and adapt their attack. You then switch to a fallback channel planned in advance (phone, separate messaging system)."},
  "Tu viens d'ouvrir une pièce jointe piégée. Remets les bons réflexes dans l'ordre : ¦ Déconnecter le poste du réseau (câble, Wi-Fi)": {"q":"You have just opened a booby-trapped attachment. Put the right reflexes in order:","e":"You isolate first to stop the spread, then you alert, provide as much information as possible and follow the instructions. Without abruptly shutting down the workstation, to preserve traces.","items":["Disconnect the workstation from the network (cable, Wi-Fi)","Notify support or the security team","Describe precisely what you did and observed","Follow the instructions received (password change, etc.)"]},
  "Quelle est la différence entre un « événement » et un « incident » de sécurité ? ¦ Un incident est repéré par un humain, un événement par un outil": {"q":"What is the difference between a security “event” and a security “incident”?","e":"SIEMs churn through millions of events (sign-ins, process launches…). Only some, after analysis, are classified as incidents because they compromise security.","a":["An incident is spotted by a human, an event by a tool","An event is an observable occurrence; an incident harms security","An incident concerns hardware, an event concerns software","An event is an incident whose severity has been confirmed"]},
  "Pendant la phase d'éradication d'un incident, on… ¦ Isole les machines touchées du réseau pour stopper la propagation": {"q":"During the eradication phase of an incident, you…","e":"Eradication eliminates what the attacker left behind (malware, accounts they created) and closes the door they used. Isolation is part of containment, restoration of recovery, and the lessons-learned review and report of the post-incident phase.","a":["Isolate the affected machines from the network to stop the spread","Restore services and data from clean backups","Remove the cause: malware, accounts created by the attacker, the exploited flaw","Write the lessons-learned review and the report for management"]},
  "Restaurer des sauvegardes sans avoir identifié le point d'entrée de l'attaquant expose à une réinfection rapide. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Restoring backups without having identified the attacker's entry point exposes you to quick reinfection.","e":"If the flaw or account used by the attacker is not dealt with, they can come back the same way. Some backups may also already contain the backdoor."},
  "Sur un poste compromis, quelles actions détruisent ou altèrent des preuves ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Lancer un nettoyage de disque": {"q":"On a compromised workstation, which actions destroy or alter evidence? (several answers)","e":"Restarting wipes the RAM, cleaning or reinstalling overwrites files and logs. Photographing the screen, by contrast, preserves a trace without touching the system.","a":["Running a disk cleanup","Restarting the machine","Photographing the screen with a smartphone","Reinstalling Windows"]},
  "Quelle agence nationale française, dont dépend le CERT-FR, traite les incidents cyber majeurs et publie des guides de gestion de crise (sigle) ? ¦ ANSSI": {"q":"Which French national agency, which CERT-FR is part of, handles major cyber incidents and publishes crisis management guides (acronym)?","e":"The ANSSI (Agence nationale de la sécurité des systèmes d'information, France's national cybersecurity agency) hosts CERT-FR and publishes many guides, including guides on cyber crisis management.","placeholder":"Acronym…","answers":["ANSSI"]},
  "Dans le cycle de réponse à incident du NIST SP 800-61 rév. 2, quelle phase suit « Détection et analyse » ? ¦ Préparation et amélioration des défenses": {"q":"In the NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 2 incident response cycle, which phase follows “Detection and analysis”?","e":"NIST 800-61 r2 has four phases: Preparation, Detection and analysis, Containment/eradication/recovery, Post-incident activity. “Identification” is a term from the SANS model.","a":["Preparation and improvement of defenses","Post-incident activity (lessons learned)","Identification and assessment of the incident","Containment, eradication and recovery"]},
  "Dans un PCA/PRA, le RTO (Recovery Time Objective) désigne… ¦ La durée maximale d'interruption admissible d'un service": {"q":"In a BCP/DRP, the RTO (Recovery Time Objective) refers to…","e":"The RTO sets how quickly a service must be back up. The acceptable data loss is the RPO; the mean time between failures is the MTBF.","a":["The maximum tolerable downtime of a service","The maximum tolerable data loss","The deadline for notifying a breach to the CNIL","The mean time between failures of a piece of equipment"]},
  "Avant d'éteindre une machine compromise, quelles données volatiles faut-il collecter en priorité ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le contenu de la mémoire vive": {"q":"Before shutting down a compromised machine, which volatile data should be collected first? (several answers)","e":"RAM, connections and processes disappear at shutdown: they reveal in-memory malware and command-and-control servers. The disk's serial number remains readable at any time.","a":["The contents of RAM","Active network connections","Running processes","The hard disk's serial number"]},
  "Selon le RGPD, une violation de données personnelles présentant un risque doit être notifiée à la CNIL si possible dans les 72 heures après en avoir pris connaissance. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Under the GDPR, a personal data breach presenting a risk must be notified to the CNIL, if possible within 72 hours of becoming aware of it.","e":"Article 33 of the GDPR requires notification without undue delay and, where feasible, no later than 72 hours, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk. Beyond that, the delay must be justified."},
  "Quelle commande Linux classique réalise une copie bit à bit d'un disque (ex. if=/dev/sdb of=disque.img) ? ¦ dd": {"q":"Which classic Linux command makes a bit-for-bit copy of a disk (e.g. if=/dev/sdb of=disque.img)?","e":"dd copies the raw blocks of a device, including empty and erased sectors. In forensics, it is used behind a write blocker, or via its variants dc3dd/dcfldd, which compute hashes.","placeholder":"Command…","answers":["dd"]},
  "La révision 3 du NIST SP 800-61 (avril 2025) organise la réponse à incident autour… ¦ Des six étapes du modèle PICERL popularisé par le SANS": {"q":"Revision 3 of NIST SP 800-61 (April 2025) organizes incident response around…","e":"Rev. 3 drops the four-phase cycle of Rev. 2 and integrates incident response into the six functions of CSF 2.0 (Govern, Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, Recover), to anchor it in overall risk management.","a":["The six steps of the PICERL model popularized by SANS","The six functions of the NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0","The 15 tactics of the MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise matrix","The four steps of the Deming wheel (Plan, Do, Check, Act)"]},
  "Le modèle SANS (PICERL), après la préparation, dans l'ordre : ¦ Identification": {"q":"The SANS model (PICERL), after preparation, in order:","e":"PICERL = Preparation, Identification, Containment, Eradication, Recovery, Lessons learned. You contain before eradicating, and you only recover once the threat has been eliminated.","items":["Identification","Containment","Eradication","Recovery","Lessons learned"]},
  "Pour acquérir la mémoire vive d'un poste Windows compromis, on utilise… ¦ Volatility, qui capture la RAM en direct sur le poste": {"q":"To acquire the RAM of a compromised Windows workstation, you use…","e":"WinPmem, DumpIt or Magnet RAM Capture produce a memory image. Volatility is an analysis framework: it processes the image, it does not capture it. Hiberfil.sys can help but does not replace a proper acquisition.","a":["Volatility, which captures RAM live on the workstation","The chkdsk /r command run from a USB stick","An acquisition tool such as WinPmem, DumpIt or Magnet RAM Capture","Hibernation followed by copying only hiberfil.sys"]},
  "Un PRA affiche un RPO de 15 minutes. Qu'est-ce que cela impose concrètement ? ¦ Un redémarrage des services en moins de 15 minutes": {"q":"A DRP shows an RPO of 15 minutes. What does this concretely require?","e":"The RPO is the maximum tolerable data loss: with 15 minutes, the last usable copy must always be less than 15 minutes old. The restart time is the RTO.","a":["Restarting services in less than 15 minutes","A full DRP test every 15 days","Informing customers within 15 minutes","Replication or backups at least every 15 minutes"]},
  "Avec NIS 2, une entité essentielle ou importante doit transmettre une alerte précoce au CSIRT ou à l'autorité compétente dans les 24 heures après avoir pris connaissance d'un incident important. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Under NIS 2, an essential or important entity must send an early warning to the CSIRT or the competent authority within 24 hours of becoming aware of a significant incident.","e":"Article 23 of NIS 2 provides for an early warning within 24 h, an incident notification within 72 h, then a final report within one month."},
  "Quels artefacts Windows aident à établir qu'un programme a été exécuté ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les fichiers Prefetch (.pf)": {"q":"Which Windows artifacts help establish that a program was executed? (several answers)","e":"Prefetch, Amcache and BAM keep traces of execution (path, dates, sometimes launch count). The hosts file is used for name resolution, not for tracking executions.","a":["Prefetch files (.pf)","The Amcache.hve hive","The hosts file","BAM (Background Activity Moderator) key entries"]},
  "Sur un volume NTFS, comment s'appelle le fichier de métadonnées qui contient une entrée pour chaque fichier et dossier (horodatages, attributs, emplacement des données) ? ¦ $MFT": {"q":"On an NTFS volume, what is the name of the metadata file that contains an entry for every file and folder (timestamps, attributes, data location)?","e":"The $MFT (Master File Table) is NTFS's central table: each file has a record there with its $STANDARD_INFORMATION and $FILE_NAME attributes. Analyzing it makes it possible to reconstruct a timeline, even for deleted files.","placeholder":"File name…","answers":["$MFT","MFT","Master File Table","$MFT (Master File Table)","mft","master file table"]},
  "Boîte Exchange Online compromise : pour savoir quels mails l'attaquant a réellement consultés, quelle action d'audit Purview analyses-tu ? ¦ New-InboxRule": {"q":"Compromised Exchange Online mailbox: to find out which emails the attacker actually viewed, which Purview audit action do you analyze?","e":"MailItemsAccessed tracks access to mailbox items (read, sync), which makes it possible to estimate the scope of a leak. New-InboxRule reveals a forwarding or hiding rule, SearchQueryInitiatedExchange the searches run in the mailbox, HardDelete a permanent deletion: useful, but they don't tell you what was read.","a":["New-InboxRule","MailItemsAccessed","HardDelete","SearchQueryInitiatedExchange"]},
  "Sur NTFS, un écart incohérent entre les horodatages $STANDARD_INFORMATION et $FILE_NAME d'un fichier peut révéler… ¦ Une défragmentation récente, qui a réécrit les métadonnées du volume": {"q":"On NTFS, an inconsistent gap between a file's $STANDARD_INFORMATION and $FILE_NAME timestamps can reveal…","e":"Timestomping tools mainly modify $STANDARD_INFORMATION, the one shown by File Explorer. $FILE_NAME, updated by the kernel, then betrays the inconsistency (e.g. an SI creation date earlier than the FN one).","a":["A recent defragmentation, which rewrote the volume's metadata","“Timestomping”: the attacker falsified the file's visible dates","A file encrypted with EFS, whose attributes are protected","A change of the system's time zone since creation"]},
  "Un mail te demande ton mot de passe « pour vérification ». Tu fais quoi ? ¦ Je le signale, c'est du phishing": {"q":"An email asks for your password “for verification”. What do you do?","e":"No legitimate service asks for your password by email. Report it using Outlook's “Report” button.","a":["I report it, it's phishing","I reply to find out who is sending it","I open the link to check the page"]},
  "Ce mail est un piège : trouve les 3 indices. ¦ De :Service Livraison <suivi@chr0nopost-livraison.info>": {"q":"This email is a trap: find the 3 clues.","e":"Three signals: the address imitates a carrier (with a zero in place of the “o”), you are asked to pay by card, and the urgency (“within 24 hours”) is meant to stop you from thinking. Polite phrases, on the other hand, prove nothing.","lines":[[{"t":"From:","c":false},{"t":"Delivery Service <suivi@chr0nopost-livraison.info>","c":true}],[{"t":"Subject: Your parcel is blocked","c":false}],[{"t":"Hello,","c":false},{"t":"your parcel could not be delivered.","c":false}],[{"t":"Fees of €1.99 must be paid by card","c":true},{"t":"within 24 hours,","c":true},{"t":"otherwise it will be sent back.","c":false}],[{"t":"Thank you for your trust, customer service.","c":false}]]},
  "Quels éléments doivent t'alerter dans un mail ? ¦ Un ton très urgent": {"q":"Which elements should alert you in an email?","e":"Urgency, a request for credentials or money, a suspicious address: this is the classic trio. The logo can be copied in two seconds: it proves nothing.","a":["A very urgent tone","A request for credentials or payment","A strange sender address","The company logo in the header"]},
  "Smishing et vishing, ce sont des attaques par… ¦ Pigeon voyageur et signaux de fumée": {"q":"Smishing and vishing are attacks carried out via…","e":"Smishing = SMS, vishing = voice (phone call). Same tactics as email phishing: urgency, authority, a request for information or payment.","a":["Carrier pigeon and smoke signals","SMS and phone call","Targeted email and premium-rate SMS"]},
  "Un mail envoyé depuis l'adresse d'un collègue est forcément sûr. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An email sent from a colleague's address is necessarily safe.","e":"False: their mailbox may have been hacked and used to trap their contacts. If the request is unusual, verify through another channel."},
  "Le « quishing », c'est… ¦ Du phishing par QR code": {"q":"“Quishing” is…","e":"A booby-trapped QR code (poster, mail, email) leads to a fake site. It often escapes anti-phishing filters, because the link doesn't appear in plain text. By SMS, it's smishing; by phone call, vishing.","a":["Phishing via QR code","Phishing via SMS","Phishing via voice call"]},
  "Signaler un mail suspect dans Outlook : remets les étapes dans l'ordre. ¦ Ne cliquer sur aucun lien ni pièce jointe": {"q":"Reporting a suspicious email in Outlook: put the steps in the right order.","e":"You don't touch anything, you select the email, then “Report” and “Report phishing”. The email is removed from your mailbox and the security team is alerted.","items":["Do not click on any link or attachment","Select the email","Click the “Report” button","Choose “Report phishing”"]},
  "Ton « PDG » t'écrit : virement urgent et confidentiel à faire aujourd'hui. Tu… ¦ Appelles le numéro indiqué dans le mail": {"q":"Your “CEO” writes to you: urgent and confidential transfer to be made today. You…","e":"This is CEO fraud. Replying to the email or calling the number provided means talking to the scammer. Always verify through a known channel (directory, in person), even if it's “urgent”.","a":["Call the number given in the email","Reply to the email to ask for details","Verify through a known channel (directory, in person)"]},
  "Contre le « consent phishing » (une appli malveillante demande des permissions) : ¦ On restreint le consentement des utilisateurs et on active le flux d'approbation admin": {"q":"Against “consent phishing” (a malicious app requests permissions):","e":"The app obtains a token without ever stealing the password: the victim passes MFA themselves, and changing their password doesn't remove the consent granted. Limiting who can consent cuts off the attack at the source.","a":["Restrict user consent and enable the admin approval workflow","Require MFA for all sign-ins via Conditional Access","Reset the passwords of the accounts targeted by the campaign"]},
  "SPF, DKIM et DMARC servent à… ¦ Chiffrer le contenu des mails de bout en bout": {"q":"SPF, DKIM and DMARC are used to…","e":"SPF lists the authorized servers, DKIM signs the emails, DMARC says what to do with emails that fail the checks.","a":["Encrypt the content of emails end to end","Authenticate the sender of a domain and limit spoofing","Force TLS encryption between mail servers"]},
  "Un phishing « adversary-in-the-middle » contourne la MFA classique en volant… ¦ Le cookie de session": {"q":"An “adversary-in-the-middle” phishing attack bypasses standard MFA by stealing…","e":"The fake site relays the real sign-in and captures the cookie. The countermeasure: phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2 keys, passkeys).","a":["The session cookie","The app's TOTP seed","The workstation's NTLM hash"]},
  "Un SMS de « ta banque » te demande de cliquer pour débloquer ton compte. Tu… ¦ Cliques, mais vérifies que la page affiche le logo de la banque": {"q":"An SMS from “your bank” asks you to click to unlock your account. You…","e":"This is smishing. Your bank will never ask you to log in through a link received by SMS. Always use a channel you know.","a":["Click, but check that the page shows the bank's logo","Don't click and contact your bank through its app or usual phone number","Reply “STOP” to the SMS to stop receiving these messages"]},
  "Le cadenas dans la barre d'adresse prouve qu'un site est honnête. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The padlock in the address bar proves that a site is honest.","e":"False: the padlock only indicates that the connection is encrypted. Most phishing sites have a padlock too. What you need to check is the address (the domain)."},
  "Un « technicien Microsoft » t'appelle : ton PC est infecté, il veut en prendre le contrôle à distance. ¦ Tu lui demandes son matricule avant de le laisser faire": {"q":"A “Microsoft technician” calls you: your PC is infected and he wants to take control of it remotely.","e":"This is the fake tech support scam (vishing). Microsoft doesn't call without a request from you. For a real problem, contact the company's IT support.","a":["You ask for his employee ID before letting him proceed","You hang up: Microsoft doesn't call unprompted","You let him do it, but you watch what he does"]},
  "Quelles informations ne faut-il jamais donner par mail ou par téléphone ? ¦ Ton mot de passe": {"q":"Which information should you never give by email or phone?","e":"Giving an MFA code to someone is opening the door to them. No legitimate service will ask you for it.","a":["Your password","A verification code received by SMS or in your MFA app","Your bank card number","The address of the company's public website"]},
  "Faux mail RH : trouve les 4 indices. ¦ De :Service RH <rh@entreprise-primes.com>": {"q":"Fake HR email: find the 4 clues.","e":"An external domain imitating the company, a request for credentials, urgency, and an .html attachment (often a fake sign-in page). The real HR department doesn't need your password to pay you.","lines":[[{"t":"From:","c":false},{"t":"HR Department <rh@entreprise-primes.com>","c":true}],[{"t":"Subject: Your year-end bonus","c":false}],[{"t":"Hello everyone,","c":false}],[{"t":"to receive your bonus, confirm your credentials","c":true},{"t":"before midnight tonight.","c":true}],[{"t":"Attachment: prime_2026.html","c":true}],[{"t":"Kind regards, the HR team","c":false}]]},
  "Le « spear phishing », c'est… ¦ Du phishing envoyé en masse à des millions de personnes à la fois": {"q":"“Spear phishing” is…","e":"The attacker does research (LinkedIn, the company website…) to write a credible message, addressed to you by name, that talks about your actual work.","a":["Phishing sent in bulk to millions of people at once","Phishing aimed at one specific person, using information about them","Phishing sent from a colleague's hacked mailbox"]},
  "Le « whaling » (chasse à la baleine) vise surtout… ¦ Les dirigeants et cadres de haut niveau": {"q":"“Whaling” mainly targets…","e":"Executives have a lot of power (transfers, access). A single compromised executive account can be very costly.","a":["Executives and senior managers","IT administrators and their privileged accounts","Animal protection associations"]},
  "Le « typosquatting », c'est… ¦ Enregistrer un nom de domaine qui ressemble au vrai (micros0ft.com)": {"q":"“Typosquatting” is…","e":"A changed letter, a zero in place of an “o”, an extra hyphen… These domains fool a hurried eye. You need to read the address letter by letter.","a":["Registering a domain name that looks like the real one (micros0ft.com)","Hiding a booby-trapped link behind a shortened URL (bit.ly…)","Buying back an expired domain to receive its old emails"]},
  "Face à un QR code sur un horodateur ou une affiche, les bons réflexes : ¦ Vérifier l'adresse qui s'affiche avant d'ouvrir le lien": {"q":"Facing a QR code on a parking meter or a poster, the right reflexes:","e":"Quishing often uses fake QR codes stuck over the real ones. At the slightest doubt, use the official application.","a":["Check the address that appears before opening the link","Beware of a sticker placed over the original","Prefer the official app or website that you type yourself","Scan and pay directly, it's faster"]},
  "Une pièce jointe .html dans un mail peut afficher une fausse page de connexion Microsoft. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An .html attachment in an email can display a fake Microsoft sign-in page.","e":"True: the file opens in the browser and perfectly imitates a sign-in page, without even going through a website."},
  "Un fournisseur t'écrit : « Nous changeons de banque, voici notre nouveau RIB. » Tu… ¦ Mets à jour le RIB, le mail vient de l'adresse habituelle": {"q":"A supplier writes to you: “We are changing banks, here are our new bank details.” You…","e":"Bank detail change fraud is very widespread, often from the supplier's real hacked mailbox. Only a call to a known contact, independent of the email, allows you to verify.","a":["Update the bank details, the email comes from the usual address","Verify by calling the supplier on their usual number, not the one in the email","Reply to the email to get written confirmation of the change"]},
  "Pour savoir qui a vraiment envoyé un mail suspect, l'admin regarde… ¦ Le nom et l'adresse affichés dans le champ De du message": {"q":"To find out who really sent a suspicious email, the admin looks at…","e":"The displayed name is easy to forge. The technical headers show the email's real path (servers traversed) and whether the sending domain is authenticated.","a":["The name and address shown in the message's From field","The message headers (servers, SPF, DKIM, DMARC)","The signature and contact details of the sender at the bottom of the email"]},
  "Côté admin, après un phishing signalé par un utilisateur : ¦ Rechercher et supprimer les copies du mail dans les autres boîtes": {"q":"On the admin side, after a phishing email reported by a user:","e":"A phishing email rarely lands with only one person. You clean up, block, and check potential victims. As for MFA, keep it!","a":["Search for and delete copies of the email in other mailboxes","Block the sender and the malicious URLs","Identify who clicked and secure those accounts","Disable MFA to simplify sign-ins"]},
  "Un mail t'invite à aller sur la vraie page Microsoft et à y saisir un code. Le danger ? ¦ Aucun, puisque l'adresse est bien celle du vrai site Microsoft": {"q":"An email invites you to go to the real Microsoft page and enter a code there. What's the danger?","e":"This is “device code phishing”: the page is real, but the code was generated by the attacker. By entering it, you give them an access token. Admins can block this flow via Conditional Access.","a":["None, since the address is the real Microsoft site's","You authorize the attacker's device to sign in to your account","Your password is captured by a fake sign-in page"]},
  "L'ingénierie sociale, c'est… ¦ La gestion des réseaux sociaux de l'entreprise": {"q":"Social engineering is…","e":"The attacker exploits trust, urgency or authority rather than a technical flaw. Phishing is its best-known form.","a":["Managing the company's social media","Manipulating a person to obtain information or access","Exploiting a software flaw to take control of a computer"]},
  "Un message sur les réseaux sociaux : « Tu as gagné un iPhone, clique vite pour le réclamer ! » ¦ Je vérifie que le compte a beaucoup d'abonnés": {"q":"A message on social media: “You've won an iPhone, click quickly to claim it!”","e":"Urgency + a too-good-to-be-true gift = trap. An account with lots of followers can be hacked or fake, and the link usually leads to a page that steals your credentials or your personal details.","a":["I check that the account has lots of followers","It's a classic scam: I don't click","I click, but without entering my bank card"]},
  "Le « pretexting », c'est… ¦ Envoyer un mail piégé avec une fausse facture en pièce jointe (souvent un PDF)": {"q":"“Pretexting” is…","e":"The attacker prepares their role, often with the help of LinkedIn or the company website. Reflex: verify the person's identity through a known channel before giving anything away.","a":["Sending a booby-trapped email with a fake invoice attached (often a PDF)","Following someone to enter a protected building without a badge","Inventing a credible scenario (fake technician, fake auditor) to obtain information"]},
  "Avec l'IA générative, les mails de phishing sans aucune faute deviennent courants. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With generative AI, phishing emails without any mistakes are becoming common.","e":"True: spelling is no longer a good indicator. Look instead at the real sender, the link, the urgency and how unusual the request is."},
  "Ton « directeur » t'appelle, voix parfaitement imitée, pour un virement urgent. La meilleure parade ? ¦ Vérifier que le numéro affiché à l'écran est bien celui du directeur": {"q":"Your “director” calls you, with a perfectly imitated voice, for an urgent transfer. The best countermeasure?","e":"Voice deepfakes need only a few seconds of recording, and the displayed number can be spoofed. A dual-approval procedure for transfers protects better than any ear.","a":["Check that the number displayed on the screen is indeed the director's","Hang up and call them back on their known number, or validate through a second channel","Listen carefully to detect a robotic voice or a slight lag"]},
  "Le « tailgating » (talonnage), c'est… ¦ Entrer dans des locaux protégés en suivant quelqu'un qui a badgé": {"q":"“Tailgating” is…","e":"Politeness makes us hold the door… Everyone badges in for themselves, and an unknown person without a badge is escorted to reception.","a":["Entering protected premises by following someone who has badged in","Following someone on social media to prepare an attack","Looking over the shoulder of someone typing their code"]},
  "Pourquoi une fraude « BEC » menée depuis la vraie boîte mail piratée d'un fournisseur est-elle si dangereuse ? ¦ Le domaine du fournisseur est imité par typosquatting, ce qui trompe les filtres": {"q":"Why is a “BEC” fraud carried out from a supplier's real, hacked mailbox so dangerous?","e":"No technical filter blocks a real email from a real account. The only reliable countermeasure: verify any change of bank details by phone, on a known number.","a":["The supplier's domain is imitated through typosquatting, which fools the filters","The emails pass through a third-party gateway that neutralizes DMARC checks","The emails are authentic: SPF, DKIM and DMARC pass, and the conversation history is real"]},
  "Quel enregistrement DNS publie la politique à appliquer aux mails qui échouent aux contrôles SPF et DKIM (none, quarantine, reject) ? ¦ DMARC": {"q":"Which DNS record publishes the policy to apply to emails that fail SPF and DKIM checks (none, quarantine, reject)?","e":"DMARC indicates what to do with emails spoofing your domain and sends reports. Goal: gradually reach p=reject.","placeholder":"Acronym","answers":["DMARC"]},
  "Faux avis de livraison : trouve les 5 indices. ¦ De : Service Livraison <suivi@colis-livraison-express.info>": {"q":"Fake delivery notice: find the 5 clues.","e":"A sender with a made-up domain, a generic greeting, a small sum to pay, artificial urgency and a link to an unknown site: the classic combo. Small amounts are used to harvest your bank card.","lines":[[{"t":"From: Delivery Service <suivi@colis-livraison-express.info>","c":true}],[{"t":"Subject: Your parcel is on hold","c":false}],[{"t":"Hello dear customer,","c":true}],[{"t":"Redelivery fees of €1.99 must be paid ","c":true},{"t":"within 24 hours, otherwise your parcel will be sent back.","c":true}],[{"t":"Pay here: https://colis-suivi.re-livraison.top/paiement","c":true}]]},
  "Pourquoi survoler un lien avec la souris avant de cliquer ? ¦ Pour lancer l'analyse du lien par l'antivirus": {"q":"Why hover over a link with the mouse before clicking?","e":"The displayed text can say “microsoft.com” while the link points elsewhere. On mobile, a long press also shows the real address.","a":["To start the link analysis by the antivirus","To see the real address it leads to","To display a preview of the page without opening it"]},
  "Si le nom affiché de l'expéditeur est « Service informatique », le mail vient forcément du service informatique. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"If the sender's display name is “IT Department”, the email necessarily comes from the IT department.","e":"False: the display name can be freely chosen. You need to look at the full address, and even that can be spoofed: when in doubt, verify through another channel."},
  "Un mail sans lien ni pièce jointe annonce le renouvellement d'un abonnement à 399 € et invite à appeler un numéro pour annuler. C'est… ¦ Du « callback phishing » : l'arnaque se poursuit au téléphone": {"q":"An email with no link or attachment announces the renewal of a €399 subscription and invites you to call a number to cancel. This is…","e":"With no link or attachment, the email gets past filters more easily. Over the phone, the fake support pushes the victim to install a remote access tool.","a":["“Callback phishing”: the scam continues over the phone","A legitimate invoice, since there is no link","Harmless advertising spam"]},
  "Dans les en-têtes d'un mail suspect, quels éléments trahissent une usurpation probable ? ¦ Un Reply-To vers un domaine différent de celui du From": {"q":"In the headers of a suspicious email, which elements point to probable spoofing?","e":"Replies go to the attacker if the Reply-To differs, and a DMARC failure indicates that the From domain is not authenticated. The Message-ID, on the other hand, is present in almost all emails.","a":["A Reply-To to a domain different from the From domain","“dmarc=fail” in Authentication-Results","The presence of a Message-ID header","A Return-Path to a domain unrelated to the displayed sender"]},
  "Mail reçu : From facturation@banque-exemple.fr ; « spf=pass smtp.mailfrom=bounce.mailer-xyz.com ; dkim=pass header.d=mailer-xyz.com ; dmarc=fail ». Pourquoi DMARC échoue-t-il ? ¦ Parce que SPF et DKIM doivent échouer tous les deux": {"q":"Email received: From facturation@banque-exemple.fr ; “spf=pass smtp.mailfrom=bounce.mailer-xyz.com ; dkim=pass header.d=mailer-xyz.com ; dmarc=fail”. Why does DMARC fail?","e":"DMARC requires that at least one passing check (SPF or DKIM) be on a domain aligned with the From domain. Here everything is validated for mailer-xyz.com, not for banque-exemple.fr: this is typical of spoofing.","a":["Because SPF and DKIM must both fail","Because the DMARC policy is necessarily p=none","Because no validated domain is aligned with the From domain"]},
  "Tu as cliqué sur un lien de phishing par erreur : mieux vaut ne rien dire à personne pour éviter les ennuis. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You clicked a phishing link by mistake: it's better to tell no one to avoid trouble.","e":"False: notify support or security right away. The faster the alert, the more the damage can be limited (password change, session revocation, blocking the link for colleagues)."},
  "Dans Microsoft Defender for Office 365, que fait la fonctionnalité « Liens fiables » (Safe Links) ? ¦ Elle chiffre les liens de bout en bout pour qu'ils ne soient pas interceptés": {"q":"In Microsoft Defender for Office 365, what does the Safe Links feature do?","e":"Safe Links analyzes the URL at the time of the click: a link that was harmless on receipt but turned malicious a few hours later is still blocked. It is protection against links “weaponized” after the fact.","a":["It encrypts links end to end so they can't be intercepted","It checks a URL's reputation at the time of the click, not only on receipt","It automatically removes all links pointing outside","It converts each link into a PDF attachment that can be read offline"]},
  "Comment s'appelle l'outil de Microsoft Defender for Office 365 qui permet de lancer des campagnes de phishing simulé pour sensibiliser les salariés ? ¦ Attack simulation training": {"q":"What is the name of the Microsoft Defender for Office 365 tool that lets you run simulated phishing campaigns to raise employee awareness?","e":"Attack simulation training sends realistic fake phishing emails, measures clicks and reports, then assigns training modules to the people who were caught.","placeholder":"Feature name…","answers":["Attack simulation training","Attack simulation","Formation à la simulation d'attaque","Formation sur la simulation d'attaque","Formation par simulation d'attaque","Exercice de simulation d'attaque","Simulation d'attaque","Attack simulator","Simulateur d'attaque","attack simulation training","attack simulation","attack simulator"]},
  "Le domaine publie : v=spf1 include:spf.protection.outlook.com -all. Quelles affirmations sont vraies ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ « -all » demande de traiter en échec (hard fail) tout serveur non listé": {"q":"The domain publishes: v=spf1 include:spf.protection.outlook.com -all. Which statements are true? (several answers)","e":"SPF lists the authorized servers and “-all” rejects the others. It checks the envelope domain (MAIL FROM), not the visible From: DMARC makes the link between them. Cryptographic signing is DKIM.","a":["“-all” asks to treat any unlisted server as a hard fail","The include authorizes Exchange Online servers to send for this domain","SPF checks the address visible in the From field displayed to the reader","This record cryptographically signs each email sent"]},
  "Pour vérifier une signature DKIM, où le serveur destinataire récupère-t-il la clé publique ? ¦ Dans l'enregistrement MX du domaine expéditeur": {"q":"To verify a DKIM signature, where does the receiving server get the public key?","e":"The DKIM signature contains the domain (d=) and the selector (s=); the recipient then queries s._domainkey.d in DNS to get the public key. In Microsoft 365, these are the two CNAMEs selector1 and selector2.","a":["In the MX record of the sending domain","In the TLS certificate presented by the sending server","In DNS, under selector._domainkey.domain","In the first Received header of the message"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre un déploiement DMARC progressif et sans casse : ¦ Publier SPF et activer DKIM pour tous les services qui envoient au nom du domaine": {"q":"Put a gradual, no-breakage DMARC deployment in the right order:","e":"You first observe (p=none) to spot forgotten legitimate tools (newsletter, CRM, invoicing), then tighten gradually. Going straight to reject would drop legitimate emails.","items":["Publish SPF and enable DKIM for all services that send on behalf of the domain","Publish DMARC with p=none and a rua address to receive reports","Analyze the reports and fix the legitimate senders that are not aligned","Switch to p=quarantine","Switch to p=reject"]},
  "Un utilisateur a signalé un mail avec le bouton « Signaler » d'Outlook. Où l'admin le retrouve-t-il dans le portail Microsoft Defender ? ¦ Dans Quarantaine, onglet E-mail des messages retenus": {"q":"A user reported an email with Outlook's “Report” button. Where does the admin find it in the Microsoft Defender portal?","e":"The Submissions page (Actions & submissions) centralizes emails reported by users: the admin can analyze them, submit them to Microsoft and send feedback to the user. Message trace shows how an email was routed, not the report.","a":["In Quarantine, the Email tab of held messages","In Submissions, the “User reported” tab","In Threat policies, the inbound anti-spam policy","In the Exchange admin center, message trace"]},
  "Dans Exchange Online, la purge automatique « zero-hour » (ZAP) peut retirer d'une boîte aux lettres un mail déjà livré s'il est reconnu comme phishing après coup. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Exchange Online, zero-hour auto purge (ZAP) can remove from a mailbox an email that has already been delivered if it is later recognized as phishing.","e":"True: ZAP acts after delivery. If signatures or reputation change, the email that already arrived is moved (to quarantine or to the junk email folder depending on the policy)."},
  "Dans une stratégie anti-hameçonnage de Defender for Office 365, la protection contre l'emprunt d'identité sert à… ¦ imposer la MFA aux comptes des dirigeants et de la compta": {"q":"In a Defender for Office 365 anti-phishing policy, impersonation protection is used to…","e":"You declare the key people (management, accounting) and your domains; Defender then spots senders that come close to them, such as “rnicrosoft.com” or a display name copied from an external address.","a":["require MFA for the accounts of executives and accounting","automatically encrypt executives' outgoing emails","block executives' sign-ins from unusual countries","detect emails imitating protected users or domains"]},
  "Dans Entra ID, quelles méthodes d'authentification sont considérées comme résistantes au phishing ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Clé de sécurité FIDO2 ou passkey": {"q":"In Entra ID, which authentication methods are considered phishing-resistant? (several answers)","e":"FIDO2/passkeys and Windows Hello for Business bind authentication to the real domain: a fake page can't replay them. Number matching reduces MFA fatigue but can still be relayed by an AiTM proxy, just like an SMS code.","a":["FIDO2 security key or passkey","Windows Hello for Business","Microsoft Authenticator notification with number matching","One-time code received by SMS"]},
  "Dans un enregistrement DMARC, quelle balise fixe la politique appliquée aux sous-domaines ? ¦ pct": {"q":"In a DMARC record, which tag sets the policy applied to subdomains?","e":"sp= (subdomain policy) applies to subdomains; without it, they inherit p=. ruf is the address for failure reports, adkim the DKIM alignment mode. pct (percentage of messages affected) is a legacy tag: RFC 9989 of May 2026, which replaces RFC 7489, removed it in favor of t= (test mode) and added np= for non-existent subdomains.","a":["pct","sp","ruf","adkim"]},
  "Que signifie adkim=s dans un enregistrement DMARC ? ¦ La signature DKIM doit utiliser une clé d'au moins 2048 bits": {"q":"What does adkim=s mean in a DMARC record?","e":"s = strict: exact match, a subdomain is not enough. In relaxed mode (r, the default), a d= such as mail.exemple.fr aligns with exemple.fr. Same logic for aspf with SPF.","a":["The DKIM signature must use a key of at least 2048 bits","DKIM is ignored: only SPF alignment counts for DMARC","The DKIM d= must be exactly the From domain","DKIM reports are sent every day to the rua address"]},
  "Ton SPF enchaîne les include: de nombreux prestataires. Au-delà de combien de requêtes DNS l'évaluation échoue-t-elle en permerror (RFC 7208) ? ¦ 5": {"q":"Your SPF record chains include: mechanisms for many providers. Beyond how many DNS queries does evaluation fail with a permerror (RFC 7208)?","e":"RFC 7208 limits to 10 the mechanisms and modifiers that trigger a DNS query (include, a, mx, ptr, exists, redirect). Beyond that: permerror, so SPF becomes unusable and DMARC can no longer rely on it.","a":["5","10","15","20"]},
  "Un domaine qui n'envoie jamais de mail n'a pas besoin d'enregistrements SPF ni DMARC, puisqu'il n'y a rien à protéger. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A domain that never sends email doesn't need SPF or DMARC records, since there is nothing to protect.","e":"False: a “dormant” domain can be spoofed like any other. You publish v=spf1 -all and a DMARC policy of p=reject to tell the whole world that any email sent in its name is illegitimate."},
  "Ton MX pointe vers une passerelle de filtrage tierce placée devant Exchange Online. Les contrôles SPF des mails entrants échouent car EOP voit l'IP de la passerelle. Quelle fonctionnalité corrige ça ? ¦ Le filtrage amélioré pour les connecteurs (Enhanced Filtering)": {"q":"Your MX points to a third-party filtering gateway placed in front of Exchange Online. SPF checks on incoming emails fail because EOP sees the gateway's IP. Which feature fixes this?","e":"Enhanced Filtering for Connectors lets Exchange Online find the real source IP behind the gateway and run SPF, DKIM and DMARC correctly again. Bypassing filtering with a mail flow rule would lose all of Defender's protection.","a":["Enhanced Filtering for Connectors","Disabling DKIM on the accepted domain","Switching your DMARC policy to p=none","Adding the gateway to a mail flow rule that bypasses filtering"]},
  "Un EDR, c'est… ¦ Un outil qui détecte les comportements suspects sur les postes et permet d'y réagir": {"q":"An EDR is…","e":"EDR (Endpoint Detection and Response) goes further than antivirus: it analyzes behavior, keeps a history and can isolate a device remotely. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint is one.","a":["A tool that detects suspicious behavior on devices and lets you respond to it","A tool that centralizes and correlates logs from all sources","A firewall that filters traffic between devices and the Internet"]},
  "À quoi sert un SIEM ? ¦ À scanner les serveurs pour trouver les failles non corrigées": {"q":"What is a SIEM used for?","e":"The SIEM gathers logs (firewall, servers, Entra ID…) and spots suspicious sequences. It is the core tool of a SOC (e.g. Microsoft Sentinel).","a":["Scanning servers to find unpatched vulnerabilities","Centralizing and correlating logs to detect incidents","Detecting and blocking malware on each device"]},
  "Le rôle d'un SOC, c'est… ¦ Surveiller en continu la sécurité, détecter et répondre aux incidents": {"q":"The role of a SOC is to…","e":"The Security Operations Center analyzes alerts, qualifies incidents and coordinates the response, often 24/7. Analysts work there in tiers (T1, T2, T3).","a":["Continuously monitor security, detect and respond to incidents","Carry out the penetration tests commissioned by management","Manage users' accounts, licenses and devices"]},
  "Les étapes de la « Cyber Kill Chain », dans l'ordre : ¦ Reconnaissance": {"q":"The steps of the “Cyber Kill Chain”, in order:","e":"This model (Lockheed Martin) breaks an attack into 7 steps. Breaking any link stops the attack, and each step leaves detectable traces.","items":["Reconnaissance","Weaponization","Delivery","Exploitation","Installation","Command and control","Actions on objectives"]},
  "Le « mouvement latéral », c'est quand l'attaquant… ¦ Obtient des droits admin sur la machine qu'il a déjà compromise": {"q":"“Lateral movement” is when the attacker…","e":"After compromising a device, the attacker looks for credentials to pivot to more interesting servers. Segmentation and least privilege slow them down.","a":["Obtains admin rights on the machine they have already compromised","Moves from machine to machine in the network after an initial compromise","Sends the stolen data to a server they control"]},
  "SOC signifie… ¦ Security Operations Console": {"q":"SOC stands for…","e":"The SOC is the team (and tools) that continuously monitors security, often 24/7, to detect and respond to attacks.","a":["Security Operations Console","Security Operations Center","Air-Conditioned Computer Room"]},
  "Un « faux positif », c'est… ¦ Une vraie attaque qui n'a pas été détectée": {"q":"A “false positive” is…","e":"Too many false positives overwhelm analysts. A confirmed alert is a true positive; the “false negative” (a real attack that went undetected) is even more dangerous.","a":["A real attack that went undetected","An alert confirmed as a real attack","An alert triggered when there is no real threat"]},
  "Les journaux (logs) servent aussi à comprendre une attaque après coup. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Logs are also used to understand an attack after the fact.","e":"True: without logs, it is impossible to know how the attacker got in and what they did. That is why they are centralized and kept for long enough."},
  "Un analyste SOC de niveau 1… ¦ Trie les alertes, écarte les faux positifs et escalade les vrais incidents": {"q":"A tier 1 SOC analyst…","e":"T1 qualifies, T2 investigates in depth, T3 does threat hunting and expert work. An ideal position to start in cyber!","a":["Triages alerts, dismisses false positives and escalates real incidents","Conducts threat hunting based on hypotheses about attackers","Performs in-depth forensic analysis of compromised machines"]},
  "Un IOC (indicateur de compromission), c'est par exemple… ¦ Une technique d'attaque répertoriée dans MITRE ATT&CK (ex. T1566)": {"q":"An IOC (indicator of compromise) is, for example…","e":"IOCs are shared between teams (CERT-FR, vendors…) so that everyone can look for the same traces on their own systems.","a":["An attack technique listed in MITRE ATT&CK (e.g. T1566)","An IP address, domain or file hash linked to a known attack","A published vulnerability with its CVE identifier and CVSS score"]},
  "Dans les journaux de sécurité Windows, l'événement 4625 signale… ¦ Une ouverture de session réussie": {"q":"In the Windows security logs, event 4625 indicates…","e":"4624 = successful logon, 4625 = failure, 4740 = account locked out. Dozens of 4625s followed by a 4624 on the same account: someone may have finally found the password.","a":["A successful sign-in","An account lockout after too many attempts","A failed sign-in"]},
  "Le référentiel MITRE ATT&CK… ¦ Répertorie les tactiques et techniques réellement utilisées par les attaquants": {"q":"The MITRE ATT&CK framework…","e":"It is the common language of SOCs: an attack is described step by step (initial access, persistence, privilege escalation…) and you check what you can detect.","a":["Lists the tactics and techniques actually used by attackers","Catalogs published vulnerabilities with their CVE identifier","Is a cyber risk management framework intended for management"]},
  "Journal de connexions M365 : trouve les 3 lignes suspectes. ¦ 08:52 · j.martin · Avignon · connexion réussie": {"q":"M365 sign-in log: find the 3 suspicious lines.","e":"Avignon then Singapore within 15 minutes: “impossible travel”. 58 failures then a success at 3 a.m.: a successful brute force. The external forwarding rule right after: the attacker is settling in to keep an eye on the emails.","lines":[[{"t":"08:52 · j.martin · Avignon · successful sign-in","c":false}],[{"t":"09:07 · j.martin · Singapore · successful sign-in","c":true}],[{"t":"09:30 · c.durand · Avignon · successful sign-in","c":false}],[{"t":"03:12 · admin · 58 failures then successful sign-in","c":true}],[{"t":"03:15 · admin · new mail forwarding rule to an external address","c":true}]]},
  "Le « threat hunting », c'est… ¦ Trier et qualifier les alertes remontées par le SIEM": {"q":"“Threat hunting” is…","e":"Example hypothesis: “an attacker would use encoded PowerShell to hide.” You then query the logs to check, even without an alert.","a":["Triaging and qualifying alerts raised by the SIEM","Testing defenses by simulating an authorized attack (red team)","Tracking down, based on hypotheses, threats that no alert has seen"]},
  "Un SOAR sert à… ¦ Automatiser la réponse aux alertes grâce à des playbooks": {"q":"A SOAR is used to…","e":"Enrich an alert, block an IP, isolate a device, open a ticket… automatically. Analysts keep their time for complex cases.","a":["Automate the response to alerts using playbooks","Centralize and correlate security logs","Inventory server vulnerabilities and prioritize them"]},
  "Chez Microsoft, la solution SIEM dans le cloud s'appelle… ¦ Microsoft Defender for Cloud": {"q":"At Microsoft, the cloud SIEM solution is called…","e":"Sentinel collects logs (M365, Entra ID, firewalls, servers…), correlates them and triggers alerts and automations. It integrates with the Microsoft Defender portal.","a":["Microsoft Defender for Cloud","Microsoft Sentinel","Microsoft Purview"]},
  "Quelles sources de journaux un SOC collecte-t-il typiquement ? ¦ Pare-feu": {"q":"Which log sources does a SOC typically collect?","e":"Network, identities and endpoints: these are the three essential angles for following an attacker end to end.","a":["Firewalls","The reception area's music playlist","Domain controllers and Entra ID","EDR on devices and servers"]},
  "Pourquoi synchroniser l'heure (NTP) de tous les équipements est-il crucial pour un SOC ? ¦ Pour envoyer les alertes pendant les heures de service des analystes": {"q":"Why is synchronizing the time (NTP) of all equipment crucial for a SOC?","e":"If the firewall is 7 minutes ahead of the server, the investigation becomes a headache. Kerberos, for its part, even refuses authentication beyond a 5-minute difference by default.","a":["To send alerts during the analysts' working hours","So that the SIEM compresses logs by time slot","Without consistent timestamps, it is impossible to correlate events and the timeline"]},
  "La « pyramide de la douleur » : de l'indicateur le plus facile à changer pour l'attaquant au plus difficile. ¦ Empreintes de fichiers (hash)": {"q":"The “Pyramid of Pain”: from the indicator easiest for the attacker to change to the hardest.","e":"Modifying a file changes its hash in a second; changing how you operate is far more costly. The higher you detect in the pyramid, the more you hinder the attacker.","items":["File hashes","IP addresses","Domain names","Network and host artifacts","Tools","Tactics, techniques and procedures (TTPs)"]},
  "Quel numéro d'événement du journal Système de Windows signale l'installation d'un nouveau service ? ¦ 7045": {"q":"Which event ID in the Windows System log indicates the installation of a new service?","e":"7045 = a service was installed on the system (source Service Control Manager). An unknown service created on a server, especially with a binary in a temp folder or an ADMIN$ share, is a classic sign of persistence or lateral movement (PsExec).","placeholder":"Number","answers":["7045"]},
  "Quel référentiel répertorie les tactiques et techniques réelles des attaquants ? ¦ MITRE ATT&CK": {"q":"Which framework lists the real tactics and techniques of attackers?","e":"MITRE ATT&CK is the common language of SOCs: each technique has an identifier, for example T1566 for phishing.","placeholder":"Framework name","answers":["MITRE ATT&CK","MITRE ATTACK","ATT&CK","ATTACK","MITRE"]},
  "Traitement d'une alerte par le SOC, dans l'ordre : ¦ Recevoir l'alerte": {"q":"How a SOC handles an alert, in order:","e":"Triage (qualification) avoids wasting time on false positives. Every alert is documented, which also helps improve detection rules.","items":["Receive the alert","Qualify it: true or false positive?","Investigate or escalate to the next tier","Close it, documenting what was done"]},
  "Quel outil gratuit de Sysinternals enrichit les journaux Windows (création de processus, connexions réseau, chargement de pilotes) ? ¦ Sysmon": {"q":"Which free Sysinternals tool enriches Windows logs (process creation, network connections, driver loading)?","e":"Sysmon writes much more detailed traces than the default logs to Event Viewer (command line, hash, parent process). It is a prime source for a SIEM.","placeholder":"Tool name…","answers":["Sysmon","System Monitor","Sysmon.exe","Sysmon64"]},
  "Une règle Sigma, c'est… ¦ Une règle de pare-feu au format propriétaire des équipements Cisco": {"q":"A Sigma rule is…","e":"Written in YAML, a Sigma rule describes a detection on logs once, then is translated into KQL, SPL, etc. Thousands of community rules are shared and mapped to MITRE ATT&CK. Patterns in files are rather the role of YARA.","a":["A firewall rule in the proprietary format of Cisco equipment","An open detection rule format, convertible for many SIEMs","An antivirus signature describing patterns in executable files"]},
  "Arbre des processus d'un poste : trouve les 2 lignes suspectes. ¦ explorer.exe → outlook.exe": {"q":"Process tree of a device: find the 2 suspicious lines.","e":"Word launching an encoded PowerShell: a classic sign of a malicious macro. A DLL run from C:\\Users\\Public, a folder accessible to everyone, is just as abnormal. The other chains are normal.","lines":[[{"t":"explorer.exe → outlook.exe","c":false}],[{"t":"winword.exe → powershell.exe -enc JABjAGwAaQBlAG4AdA…","c":true}],[{"t":"services.exe → svchost.exe -k netsvcs","c":false}],[{"t":"rundll32.exe C:\\Users\\Public\\maj.dll,Start","c":true}],[{"t":"explorer.exe → msedge.exe","c":false}]]},
  "Que fait cette requête KQL ? SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) | where ResultType != \"0\" | summarize Echecs = count() by IPAddress | where Echecs > 50 ¦ Elle liste les comptes créés dans l'heure": {"q":"What does this KQL query do? SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) | where ResultType != \"0\" | summarize Echecs = count() by IPAddress | where Echecs > 50","e":"A ResultType other than 0 means a failed sign-in. Grouping by IP and filtering above a threshold brings out brute force and password spraying. A query blocks nothing: you need an analytics rule or a playbook.","a":["It lists the accounts created in the last hour","It automatically blocks the IP addresses with failures","It lists the IPs with more than 50 failed sign-ins in the last hour"]},
  "Sysmon remonte un événement 10 (ProcessAccess) : un processus inhabituel ouvre lsass.exe avec des droits de lecture mémoire. Cela évoque… ¦ T1003.001 : vol d'identifiants dans la mémoire de LSASS": {"q":"Sysmon raises an event 10 (ProcessAccess): an unusual process opens lsass.exe with memory read rights. This suggests…","e":"LSASS keeps authentication secrets in memory; tools such as Mimikatz extract them from there. Countermeasures: Credential Guard, LSA protection (RunAsPPL) and EDR attack surface reduction rules.","a":["T1003.001: credential theft from LSASS memory","T1021.002: lateral movement via SMB shares","T1566.001: phishing with a malicious attachment"]},
  "Dans un SIEM, « corréler » des événements, c'est… ¦ relier des événements de sources différentes pour repérer une attaque": {"q":"In a SIEM, “correlating” events means…","e":"An isolated failed sign-in is nothing; ten failures followed by a success from an unusual country and then the creation of a forwarding rule is an alert. Normalization prepares the data, correlation assembles these pieces coming from different logs.","a":["linking events from different sources to spot an attack","normalizing them so that all sources share the same fields","deduplicating them to reduce the volume stored in the SIEM","archiving them in cheaper storage after 90 days"]},
  "Que signifie l'acronyme SIEM ? ¦ System Integrated Event Monitor": {"q":"What does the acronym SIEM stand for?","e":"The SIEM collects, centralizes and analyzes security logs (events) from the whole information system to detect threats and keep records.","a":["System Integrated Event Monitor","Security Information and Event Management","Secure Internet Endpoint Manager","Security Incident and Emergency Mode"]},
  "Un « faux négatif » est une attaque réelle qui n'a déclenché aucune alerte. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A “false negative” is a real attack that triggered no alert.","e":"This is the most dangerous case: the attack goes unnoticed. A false positive is the opposite, an alert triggered by legitimate activity."},
  "Pourquoi un SOC surveille-t-il souvent 24 h/24 et 7 j/7 ? ¦ Parce que les antivirus se mettent en veille hors des heures de bureau": {"q":"Why does a SOC often monitor 24/7?","e":"Attackers take advantage of periods when teams are absent (nights, weekends, public holidays) to act unseen. Continuous monitoring reduces the time between intrusion and response.","a":["Because antivirus software goes to sleep outside office hours","Because the law requires it for all companies, regardless of size","Because attackers often act at night and on weekends, when nobody is watching","Because analysts sleep better at the office"]},
  "Dans l'Observateur d'événements Windows, quel journal contient les ouvertures et échecs de session ? ¦ Application": {"q":"In the Windows Event Viewer, which log contains sign-in successes and failures?","e":"The Security log records audit events: sign-ins, failures, account changes… The System log mostly concerns drivers and services.","a":["Application","System","Setup","Security"]},
  "Quels comportements peuvent déclencher une alerte dans un SOC ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Une connexion depuis un pays où l'entreprise n'a aucune activité": {"q":"Which behaviors can trigger an alert in a SOC? (several answers)","e":"The SOC looks for the unusual: improbable location, bursts of failures, permission changes outside normal hours. Opening a document from your team is normal activity.","a":["A sign-in from a country where the company has no activity","Dozens of failed sign-ins within a few minutes","A user opening a Word file shared by their team","An account added in the middle of the night to the administrators group"]},
  "Quel outil intégré à Windows permet de consulter les journaux d'événements ? ¦ Observateur d'événements": {"q":"Which tool built into Windows lets you view event logs?","e":"Event Viewer (eventvwr.msc) displays the Application, Security, System logs and many others. It is the first reflex when investigating a machine.","placeholder":"Tool name","answers":["Observateur d'événements","Observateur d evenements","Event Viewer","eventvwr","eventvwr.msc","event viewer"]},
  "La « fatigue d'alerte » (alert fatigue), c'est… ¦ des analystes noyés sous les faux positifs, qui ratent les vraies alertes": {"q":"“Alert fatigue” is…","e":"Too many irrelevant alerts wear down attention: analysts process them quickly and let real threats through. Hence the importance of tuning rules and reducing false positives.","a":["analysts drowning in false positives who miss the real alerts","users' weariness with Windows update notifications","a SIEM server that slows down, saturated by the volume of logs","the wear of SOC screens that have been on 24 hours a day for years"]},
  "Un « playbook » dans un SOC, c'est… ¦ la liste des jeux vidéo interdits sur les postes de travail": {"q":"A “playbook” in a SOC is…","e":"The playbook guides the analyst step by step (checks, what to collect, containment actions, escalation) for a given type of alert. It ensures a fast and consistent response, and can be automated in a SOAR.","a":["the list of video games banned on workstations","a written procedure of the actions to take for a type of incident","the schedule of on-call duties and night teams of the SOC","the service level agreement (SLA) signed with the SIEM vendor"]},
  "Dans le journal Sécurité de Windows, l'événement 4624 signale… ¦ un échec d'ouverture de session": {"q":"In the Windows Security log, event 4624 indicates…","e":"4624 = successful sign-in, 4625 = failure, 4634 = logoff, 4740 = account locked out. A series of 4625 followed by a 4624 for the same account deserves a closer look.","a":["a failed sign-in","a session logoff","a successful sign-in","an account lockout"]},
  "Quel événement du journal Sécurité Windows indique la création d'un compte utilisateur ? ¦ 4740": {"q":"Which Windows Security log event indicates the creation of a user account?","e":"4720: a user account was created. An unexpected account creation, especially followed by an addition to a privileged group, is a classic sign of persistence.","a":["4740","4624","4688","4720"]},
  "L'événement 1102 du journal Sécurité indique que le journal d'audit a été effacé. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Event 1102 of the Security log indicates that the audit log was cleared.","e":"Clearing logs is a trace-removal technique (MITRE ATT&CK T1685.005 since v19 of April 2026, formerly T1070.001). A 1102 outside a planned operation must trigger an investigation."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le parcours d'un événement jusqu'à l'alerte dans un SIEM : ¦ L'événement est généré sur la source (poste, serveur, pare-feu)": {"q":"Put in order the path of an event up to the alert in a SIEM:","e":"Without collection or normalization, no rule can work: a badly parsed field (IP, user) is enough to make a detection blind. Checking that sources are reporting properly is part of the SOC's job.","items":["The event is generated on the source (workstation, server, firewall)","It is collected and transported to the SIEM","It is parsed and normalized (parsing)","Detection rules correlate it with other events","An alert is created for the analysts"]},
  "Quels éléments t'aident à qualifier une alerte en faux positif ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ L'action correspond à une intervention planifiée et documentée (ticket de changement)": {"q":"Which elements help you classify an alert as a false positive? (several answers)","e":"A false positive is classified with evidence of legitimacy: documented change, business context, known tool and origin. A low severity proves nothing: some attacks begin with discreet signals.","a":["The action matches a planned and documented intervention (change ticket)","The user confirms and the activity is consistent with their role","The alert has a “low” severity","The flagged tool is the IT administration software, launched from its usual server"]},
  "Quel numéro d'événement du journal Sécurité Windows enregistre la création d'un processus ? ¦ 4688": {"q":"Which Windows Security log event number records the creation of a process?","e":"Event 4688 (to be enabled via the audit policy, with the option to include the command line) traces every process launched. Sysmon provides the enriched equivalent with its event 1.","placeholder":"Event number","answers":["4688"]},
  "Une règle de détection génère des dizaines de faux positifs par jour. Quelle est la bonne réaction ? ¦ Analyser les cas puis l'affiner avec des exclusions ciblées": {"q":"A detection rule generates dozens of false positives per day. What is the right reaction?","e":"Disabling a rule or filtering its logs opens a blind spot. Instead, adjust it with precise exclusions (service account, known server), thresholds or context, documented, while checking that it still detects the targeted malicious behavior.","a":["Analyze the cases, then tune it with targeted exclusions","Disable it while the team catches up on its backlog","Set its alerts to low severity so they are less bothersome","Filter out at the source the logs that trigger it, to lighten the SIEM"]},
  "Dans un événement 4624, le « Logon Type » 10 correspond à… ¦ une connexion réseau (accès à un partage SMB)": {"q":"In a 4624 event, “Logon Type” 10 corresponds to…","e":"Type 2 = interactive (keyboard), 3 = network, 5 = service, 10 = RemoteInteractive (RDP). Type 10 logons to user workstations can betray lateral movement.","a":["a network logon (access to an SMB share)","a Remote Desktop logon (RemoteInteractive)","a keyboard sign-in on the machine","the start of a service"]},
  "Quels opérateurs existent réellement dans le langage KQL ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ summarize": {"q":"Which operators really exist in the KQL language? (several answers)","e":"where filters, project chooses the columns and summarize aggregates (summarize count() by …). There is no groupby operator in KQL: grouping is done with the by clause of summarize.","a":["summarize","where","project","groupby"]},
  "Quel numéro d'événement Windows signale l'ajout d'un membre à un groupe de sécurité global (comme « Admins du domaine ») ? ¦ 4728": {"q":"Which Windows event number signals the addition of a member to a global security group (such as “Domain Admins”)?","e":"4728: member added to a global security group. The equivalents are 4732 for a local group and 4756 for a universal group. Monitoring these additions on privileged groups is a basic detection.","placeholder":"Event number","answers":["4728"]},
  "Dans Sysmon, l'événement 3 correspond à une connexion réseau. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Sysmon, event 3 corresponds to a network connection.","e":"Sysmon: 1 = process creation, 3 = network connection, 11 = file creation, 22 = DNS query. Event 3 lets you link an outbound connection to the process that initiated it."},
  "Sur un contrôleur de domaine, l'événement 4768 correspond à… ¦ une demande de ticket de service Kerberos": {"q":"On a domain controller, event 4768 corresponds to…","e":"4768 = TGT request (AS), 4769 = service ticket request (TGS), 4771 = pre-authentication failure, 4776 = NTLM credential validation by the DC. Telling them apart is essential for hunting Kerberos attacks.","a":["a Kerberos service ticket request","a Kerberos pre-authentication failure","a Kerberos TGT request","an NTLM credential validation"]},
  "En KQL, quelle est la différence entre les opérateurs « has » et « contains » ? ¦ Aucune : « has » est un simple alias de « contains » en KQL": {"q":"In KQL, what is the difference between the “has” and “contains” operators?","e":"“has” searches for a whole term (delimited by non-alphanumeric characters) using the index, hence better performance. “contains” also finds a fragment in the middle of a word. Both ignore case; their _cs variants respect it.","a":["None: “has” is simply an alias of “contains” in KQL","“contains” only applies to dynamic arrays, “has” to strings","“has” is case-sensitive, “contains” never is","“has” searches for a whole term via the index, “contains” for a substring"]},
  "Sysmon remonte des événements 8 (CreateRemoteThread) : un processus crée un thread dans un autre processus. Cela évoque surtout… ¦ une injection de code dans un processus légitime": {"q":"Sysmon raises events 8 (CreateRemoteThread): a process creates a thread in another process. This mostly suggests…","e":"Creating a thread in another process is a classic injection technique (MITRE ATT&CK T1055) to run malicious code under the identity of a trusted process. Some legitimate software does it too, hence the need to add context.","a":["code injection into a legitimate process","a Windows update in progress","a simple background backup","a graphics driver problem"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre cette requête KQL qui compte les échecs de connexion par compte sur 24 h : ¦ SecurityEvent": {"q":"Put in order this KQL query that counts failed sign-ins per account over 24 h:","e":"You start from the table, filter early (faster), aggregate, then sort. The filter on EventID must come before summarize, which keeps only the grouping and aggregate columns, and the sort uses the Echecs column created by summarize.","items":["SecurityEvent","| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h) and EventID == 4625","| summarize Echecs = count() by TargetAccount","| order by Echecs desc"]},
  "Quel numéro d'événement du journal Sécurité Windows signale la création d'une tâche planifiée ? ¦ 4698": {"q":"Which Windows Security log event number signals the creation of a scheduled task?","e":"4698: a scheduled task was created (the “Other Object Access Events” audit is required). Scheduled tasks are a very common persistence mechanism (MITRE ATT&CK T1053.005), to be hunted regularly.","placeholder":"Event number","answers":["4698"]},
  "Une mise à jour de sécurité est disponible sur ton PC. Tu… ¦ L'installes rapidement : elle corrige des failles connues": {"q":"A security update is available on your PC. You…","e":"As soon as a vulnerability is published, attackers look for unpatched machines. Updating quickly means closing the door before they arrive.","a":["Install it quickly: it fixes known vulnerabilities","Postpone it for a month: your antivirus is enough to protect you","Ignore it: it only brings new wallpapers"]},
  "Une « CVE », c'est… ¦ Un identifiant public attribué à une vulnérabilité connue": {"q":"A “CVE” is…","e":"Every published vulnerability receives an identifier (e.g. CVE-2024-XXXX). Teams use it to know which machines to fix first. The severity score from 0 to 10 is the CVSS.","a":["A public identifier assigned to a known vulnerability","A severity score assigned to a flaw, from 0 to 10","A patch bulletin published by the software vendor"]},
  "La « défense en profondeur » consiste à… ¦ Inspecter les paquets en profondeur (DPI) sur le pare-feu": {"q":"“Defense in depth” consists of…","e":"Firewall, MFA, EDR, backups, awareness training… If one layer falls, the next ones slow down or stop the attack. Deep packet inspection (DPI) is just one of these layers.","a":["Inspecting packets in depth (DPI) on the firewall","Stacking several independent layers of security","Concentrating the effort on a strict perimeter firewall"]},
  "Pourquoi désinstaller les logiciels qu'on n'utilise plus ? ¦ Pour faire de la place à ta collection de fonds d'écran": {"q":"Why uninstall software you no longer use?","e":"Every piece of software is a potential door. Reducing the “attack surface” is the basis of hardening.","a":["To make room for your wallpaper collection","Less software means fewer possible vulnerabilities","Unused software eventually blocks updates"]},
  "Un logiciel qui n'est plus mis à jour par son éditeur (fin de support) reste sûr tant qu'il fonctionne. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Software that is no longer updated by its vendor (end of support) remains safe as long as it works.","e":"False: new vulnerabilities will never be fixed again. Example: Windows 10, whose standard support ended in October 2025."},
  "Le score CVSS indique… ¦ La probabilité qu'une faille soit exploitée dans les 30 jours": {"q":"The CVSS score indicates…","e":"From 9.0, it is critical. But context matters too: a medium flaw actively exploited on an exposed server comes before a critical flaw on an isolated machine. The probability of exploitation is the EPSS.","a":["The probability that a vulnerability will be exploited within 30 days","The fix urgency set by the vendor, from 1 to 5","The severity of a vulnerability, on a scale from 0 to 10"]},
  "Un test d'intrusion (pentest)… ¦ Simule une attaque, avec autorisation écrite, pour trouver les failles": {"q":"A penetration test (pentest)…","e":"Without the owner's written authorization, it is an intrusion punishable by law (article 323-1 of the French Penal Code). With it, it is a fascinating career. Listing CVEs is a vulnerability scan; checking against a standard is a configuration audit.","a":["Simulates an attack, with written authorization, to find vulnerabilities","Analyzes installed versions to list known CVEs","Checks that configurations comply with a given standard"]},
  "Durcir (« hardening ») un serveur, c'est… ¦ Le mettre dans une baie verrouillée, en salle à accès contrôlé": {"q":"Hardening a server means…","e":"ANSSI guides and CIS Benchmarks provide lists of recognized settings, which can be checked and audited.","a":["Putting it in a locked rack, in an access-controlled room","Disabling unnecessary services, ports and accounts, and securing its configuration","Scheduling a full, tested backup every night"]},
  "Quelles mesures réduisent la surface d'attaque d'un poste Windows ? ¦ Retirer les droits administrateur locaux aux utilisateurs": {"q":"Which measures reduce the attack surface of a Windows workstation?","e":"Without admin rights, a tricked user cannot install much. Session lock, on the other hand, must stay enabled!","a":["Removing local administrator rights from users","Enabling Windows Firewall","Disabling session lock","Applying updates"]},
  "Le catalogue KEV de la CISA (agence américaine) liste… ¦ Les CVE notées critiques (CVSS 9 ou plus) de l'année": {"q":"The CISA (US agency) KEV catalog lists…","e":"Thousands of CVEs are published every year: it is impossible to fix everything at once. The KEV helps prioritize what attackers actually use. CERT-FR also publishes its alerts.","a":["The year's CVEs rated critical (CVSS 9 or higher)","Software at end of support to be removed from the fleet","Actively exploited vulnerabilities, to be fixed first"]},
  "Windows LAPS sert à… ¦ Donner à chaque poste un mot de passe admin local unique et renouvelé": {"q":"Windows LAPS is used to…","e":"Without LAPS, the same local admin password on all workstations lets an attacker hop from machine to machine (lateral movement).","a":["Give each workstation a unique, regularly rotated local admin password","Disable the built-in local administrator account on each workstation","Store BitLocker recovery keys in Active Directory"]},
  "Exposer le bureau à distance (RDP, port 3389) directement sur Internet est dangereux car… ¦ Le protocole RDP ne chiffre pas les sessions par défaut": {"q":"Exposing remote desktop (RDP, port 3389) directly to the Internet is dangerous because…","e":"RDP does encrypt the session: the danger is its exposure. Go through a VPN with MFA or a secure gateway, and never open RDP to the whole Internet.","a":["The RDP protocol does not encrypt sessions by default","It is a massive target for brute force and exploits (ransomware)","Port 3389 bypasses the server's Windows Firewall"]},
  "Serveur exposé sur Internet : trouve les 3 réglages dangereux. ¦ Port 443 (HTTPS) ouvert pour le site web": {"q":"Server exposed to the Internet: find the 3 dangerous settings.","e":"Exposed RDP + guessable password + unpatched server: attackers' winning trio. HTTPS open for a website and an active firewall are normal.","lines":[[{"t":"Port 443 (HTTPS) open for the website","c":false}],[{"t":"Port 3389 (RDP) open to the whole Internet","c":true}],[{"t":"“Administrator” account with the password “Admin2024”","c":true}],[{"t":"Windows Firewall: enabled","c":false}],[{"t":"Automatic updates: disabled since 2023","c":true}]]},
  "Pourquoi segmenter le réseau (VLAN d'administration, serveurs, postes, invités) ? ¦ Pour pouvoir se passer de pare-feu entre les zones": {"q":"Why segment the network (administration VLAN, servers, workstations, guests)?","e":"The guest Wi-Fi must never see the servers, and administration interfaces are only reachable from a dedicated network.","a":["To be able to do without firewalls between zones","To assign IP addresses without a DHCP server","To limit the lateral movement of a compromised machine"]},
  "Le modèle de « tiering » d'Active Directory… ¦ Cloisonne les comptes admin en niveaux (0 : DC, 1 : serveurs, 2 : postes)": {"q":"The Active Directory “tiering” model…","e":"A domain admin never signs in to a user workstation: otherwise their credentials could be stolen there. Microsoft has evolved it into the “Enterprise Access Model”. The order local, site, domain, OU is how GPOs are applied.","a":["Separates admin accounts into levels (0: DCs, 1: servers, 2: workstations)","Distributes domain controllers into levels (site, region, forest)","Ranks GPOs by priority order (local, site, domain, OU)"]},
  "Le score EPSS d'une vulnérabilité estime… ¦ Sa gravité technique, sur une échelle de 0 à 10": {"q":"A vulnerability's EPSS score estimates…","e":"CVSS measures severity, EPSS the probability of exploitation. Combined with the KEV catalog, they help decide what to fix first.","a":["Its technical severity, on a scale from 0 to 10","The probability that it will be exploited in the next 30 days","The number of public exploits listed for this vulnerability"]},
  "Une nouvelle caméra connectée utilise l'identifiant « admin » et le mot de passe « admin ». Tu… ¦ Les gardes : la caméra n'est joignable que depuis ton Wi-Fi": {"q":"A new connected camera uses the username “admin” and the password “admin”. You…","e":"Default credentials are public and tested en masse by bots: the Mirai botnet infected hundreds of thousands of connected devices this way.","a":["Keep them: the camera can only be reached from your Wi-Fi","Change them upon installation, with a strong password","Write them on a label stuck under the camera"]},
  "Un scanner de vulnérabilités (Nessus, OpenVAS…) exploite les failles trouvées pour prouver qu'on peut entrer dans le système. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A vulnerability scanner (Nessus, OpenVAS…) exploits the flaws it finds to prove that one can get into the system.","e":"False: it inventories known vulnerabilities (versions, configurations) without exploiting them. It is the penetration test, covered by written authorization, that goes as far as exploitation."},
  "Le « Patch Tuesday » de Microsoft a lieu… ¦ Tous les mardis de chaque mois": {"q":"Microsoft's “Patch Tuesday” takes place…","e":"Microsoft then publishes its monthly security patches. A critical, actively exploited vulnerability may nevertheless receive an emergency (“out-of-band”) fix.","a":["Every Tuesday of each month","On the first Tuesday of each month","On the second Tuesday of each month"]},
  "Laquelle de ces failles faut-il corriger en premier ? ¦ CVSS 9,8 sur un poste isolé, sans exploit public connu": {"q":"Which of these vulnerabilities should be fixed first?","e":"The CVSS score alone is not enough: an actively exploited vulnerability (KEV) on an exposed device comes before a theoretical one. You cross-reference severity, real-world exploitation (KEV, EPSS) and exposure.","a":["CVSS 9.8 on an isolated workstation, with no known public exploit","CVSS 8.1 on a VPN exposed to the Internet, listed in the KEV catalog","CVSS 7.5 on a test server that has been off for several months"]},
  "En CVSS v4.0, par quoi la métrique « Scope » de la v3.1 est-elle remplacée ? ¦ Par la métrique Exploit Maturity du nouveau groupe Threat": {"q":"In CVSS v4.0, what replaces the v3.1 “Scope” metric?","e":"v4.0 separately assesses confidentiality, integrity and availability of the vulnerable system (VC/VI/VA) and of subsequent systems (SC/SI/SA). It also adds Attack Requirements and renames the Temporal group to Threat.","a":["The Exploit Maturity metric of the new Threat group","The EPSS score, now built into the base score calculation","Separate impacts: vulnerable system and subsequent systems"]},
  "Une « vulnérabilité » informatique, c'est… ¦ Un virus qui se propage d'un poste à l'autre par clé USB": {"q":"An IT “vulnerability” is…","e":"A vulnerability is a flaw (bug, misconfiguration, default password…). An attack or malware exploits it; the vulnerability itself exists before the attack.","a":["A virus that spreads from one workstation to another via USB stick","An attack carried out against a website or a server","A weakness in software that an attacker can exploit","Software that protects the workstation against hackers"]},
  "Un « correctif » (ou patch), c'est… ¦ Un antivirus spécialisé dans les ransomwares": {"q":"A “fix” (or patch) is…","e":"The vendor releases a patch when it repairs a vulnerability or a bug. Installing it quickly closes the door before attackers exploit it.","a":["An antivirus specialized in ransomware","An update that fixes a bug or a security vulnerability","A backup copy of your files","A temporary password sent by support"]},
  "Seul Windows a besoin de mises à jour de sécurité : les applications comme le navigateur ou le lecteur PDF n'en ont pas besoin. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Only Windows needs security updates: applications like the browser or the PDF reader don't need them.","e":"Browsers, PDF readers, office suites and plugins are very frequent targets. All installed applications must be kept up to date."},
  "Ton PC affiche « Redémarrer pour terminer l'installation des mises à jour ». Pourquoi ne pas repousser indéfiniment ? ¦ Parce que le PC s'éteindra tout seul au bout de 24 h sans prévenir": {"q":"Your PC shows “Restart to finish installing updates”. Why not postpone indefinitely?","e":"Until the machine has restarted, the patched system files are often not yet in place: the vulnerability remains open. Restart as soon as possible, for example at the end of the day.","a":["Because the PC will shut down on its own after 24 hours without warning","Because Windows will delete the downloaded update after a week","Because many patches only apply on restart","Because restarting frees up disk space"]},
  "Quels éléments doivent être mis à jour régulièrement ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le système d'exploitation": {"q":"Which items must be updated regularly? (several answers)","e":"Systems, applications, extensions and firmware contain code that can have vulnerabilities. A Word document is not software: there is nothing to “patch”.","a":["The operating system","The web browser and its extensions","The firmware of the router or network equipment","Word documents that are already saved"]},
  "Pourquoi éviter d'utiliser un compte administrateur pour ton travail quotidien ? ¦ Un maliciel lancé par erreur obtiendrait les droits administrateur": {"q":"Why avoid using an administrator account for your daily work?","e":"A program inherits the rights of whoever launches it. With a standard account, malware cannot modify the system as easily: this is the principle of least privilege.","a":["Malware launched by mistake would obtain administrator rights","An administrator account makes the PC slower","An administrator account cannot read its emails","An administrator account has no Internet access"]},
  "Sous Windows 11, quelle rubrique des Paramètres permet d'installer les mises à jour ? ¦ Windows Update": {"q":"In Windows 11, which Settings section lets you install updates?","e":"Settings > Windows Update lets you check for and install updates. In companies, they are often managed by IT (Intune, WSUS…).","placeholder":"Name…","answers":["Windows Update"]},
  "Un antivirus à jour suffit à protéger un PC dont le système d'exploitation n'est plus mis à jour. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An up-to-date antivirus is enough to protect a PC whose operating system is no longer updated.","e":"Antivirus does not fix operating system vulnerabilities. An unpatched OS remains exploitable, sometimes without any malicious file being dropped."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le traitement d'une vulnérabilité : ¦ Identifier la vulnérabilité (scan, alerte de l'éditeur)": {"q":"Put the handling of a vulnerability in order:","e":"You detect, assess to prioritize, fix, then check (new scan) that the fix is effective.","items":["Identify the vulnerability (scan, vendor alert)","Assess its severity and the affected systems","Apply the patch or a workaround","Verify that the vulnerability is really fixed"]},
  "En CVSS v3.1, un score de base de 9,0 correspond à quelle sévérité ? ¦ Élevée": {"q":"In CVSS v3.1, a base score of 9.0 corresponds to which severity?","e":"CVSS v3.1 scale: Low 0.1-3.9, Medium 4.0-6.9, High 7.0-8.9, Critical 9.0-10.0. A 9.0 is therefore just barely critical.","a":["High","Critical","Medium","Low"]},
  "Sous Debian ou Ubuntu, quelle commande rafraîchit la liste des paquets puis installe les mises à jour ? ¦ sudo apt install --all": {"q":"On Debian or Ubuntu, which command refreshes the package list and then installs updates?","e":"apt update downloads the list of available versions, apt upgrade installs the updates. Without a prior update, apt does not see the new patches.","a":["sudo apt install --all","sudo apt refresh && sudo apt install","sudo dpkg --update-all","sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade"]},
  "Désactiver le protocole SMBv1 fait partie des mesures de durcissement recommandées sur Windows. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Disabling the SMBv1 protocol is one of the recommended hardening measures on Windows.","e":"SMBv1 is obsolete and was massively exploited (WannaCry via EternalBlue). It is no longer installed by default on recent versions of Windows."},
  "Quels protocoles transmettent les identifiants en clair et doivent être remplacés ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Telnet": {"q":"Which protocols transmit credentials in clear text and must be replaced? (several answers)","e":"Telnet, FTP and HTTP encrypt nothing: an attacker on the network can read passwords. They are replaced by SSH, SFTP/FTPS and HTTPS.","a":["Telnet","FTP","SSH","HTTP for a login page"]},
  "Quel outil open source de référence scanne les ports ouverts d'une machine (option -sV pour détecter les versions) ? ¦ nmap": {"q":"Which reference open-source tool scans a machine's open ports (option -sV to detect versions)?","e":"Nmap discovers hosts, open ports and service versions: the basis for measuring your attack surface. Only use it on systems you are authorized to scan.","placeholder":"Tool name…","answers":["nmap"]},
  "Par rapport à un scan non authentifié, un scan de vulnérabilités authentifié (avec identifiants)… ¦ Voit les logiciels et correctifs installés, donc détecte plus de failles": {"q":"Compared with an unauthenticated scan, an authenticated vulnerability scan (with credentials)…","e":"Logged in to the machine, the scanner reads the exact versions and installed KBs instead of guessing from the network. It is still a scan: it does not exploit vulnerabilities.","a":["Sees the installed software and patches, so detects more vulnerabilities","Is stealthier on the network, but detects fewer vulnerabilities","Exploits the vulnerabilities found to confirm they are real","Only works on servers, not on workstations"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet PowerShell native liste les correctifs (KB) installés sur une machine Windows ? ¦ Get-HotFix": {"q":"Which native PowerShell cmdlet lists the patches (KBs) installed on a Windows machine?","e":"Get-HotFix queries the WMI class Win32_QuickFixEngineering. It does not show everything (some cumulative or component updates do not appear in it), hence the value of dedicated tools.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Get-HotFix"]},
  "Le vecteur CVSS v3.1 « AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N » décrit une faille… ¦ Exploitable uniquement en local avec un compte administrateur": {"q":"The CVSS v3.1 vector “AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N” describes a vulnerability that is…","e":"AV:N = network vector, AC:L = low complexity, PR:N = no privileges, UI:N = no interaction. This is the profile of “wormable” vulnerabilities, to be fixed urgently.","a":["Exploitable only locally with an administrator account","Exploitable over the network but requiring a click from the victim","Exploitable remotely, easily, with no privileges and no click from the victim","Exploitable with physical access and high complexity"]},
  "Dans les CIS Benchmarks, le profil « Level 1 »… ¦ Est réservé aux environnements classifiés de défense et aux OIV": {"q":"In the CIS Benchmarks, the “Level 1” profile…","e":"Level 1 groups prudent settings that are not very disruptive for users. Level 2 goes further (defense in depth) at the risk of limiting some features.","a":["Is reserved for classified defense environments and critical infrastructure operators","Matches the default configuration shipped by the vendor","Requires hardware encryption of all disks and backups","Aims at a security baseline that is widely applicable, with little impact on usage"]},
  "Quels réglages de sshd_config font partie du durcissement d'un serveur SSH ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ PermitRootLogin no": {"q":"Which sshd_config settings are part of hardening an SSH server? (several answers)","e":"Forbidding direct root login, enforcing keys and limiting attempts reduce brute-force risks. Enabling X11 forwarding, on the contrary, increases the attack surface.","a":["PermitRootLogin no","PasswordAuthentication no (key-based authentication)","X11Forwarding yes","MaxAuthTries limited (for example 3)"]},
  "Microsoft Defender Vulnerability Management s'appuie principalement sur le capteur Defender for Endpoint pour inventorier logiciels et vulnérabilités : pas besoin de déployer un scanner réseau pour les appareils intégrés. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Microsoft Defender Vulnerability Management relies mainly on the Defender for Endpoint sensor to inventory software and vulnerabilities: there is no need to deploy a network scanner for onboarded devices.","e":"The inventory is continuously reported by the sensor built into onboarded workstations and servers, giving an up-to-date view without scan windows."},
  "Gestion des correctifs en entreprise, dans l'ordre : ¦ Inventorier les actifs et leurs versions": {"q":"Patch management in a company, in order:","e":"Without an inventory, you don't know what to patch. You prioritize, test to avoid regressions, deploy gradually, then measure what remains unpatched.","items":["Inventory assets and their versions","Prioritize patches (criticality, exposure, active exploitation)","Test on a pilot group","Deploy to production in waves","Check compliance (deployment rate)"]},
  "Les règles ASR (Attack Surface Reduction) de Microsoft Defender… ¦ Bloquent des comportements à risque, comme une macro qui lance un processus": {"q":"Microsoft Defender's ASR (Attack Surface Reduction) rules…","e":"ASR rules target common attacker techniques (an Office macro launching a child process, obfuscated scripts, credential theft from LSASS…). Deploy them in audit mode first before blocking.","a":["Block risky behaviors, such as a macro that launches a process","Form a scanner that finds unnecessary open ports on the workstation","Are a web application firewall (WAF) that protects IIS sites","Automate workstation backup to counter ransomware"]},
  "En CVSS v4.0, comment note-t-on un score calculé avec les métriques de base et de menace (Threat) ? ¦ CVSS-BT": {"q":"In CVSS v4.0, how is a score calculated with the Base and Threat metrics written?","e":"v4.0 requires stating the groups used: CVSS-B (base), CVSS-BT (base + threat), CVSS-BE (base + environmental), CVSS-BTE (all three). CVSS-TE does not exist.","a":["CVSS-BT","CVSS-BE","CVSS-TE","CVSS-BTE"]},
  "Sous Linux, quelle valeur de kernel.randomize_va_space active l'ASLR complète, tas (brk) compris ? ¦ 2": {"q":"On Linux, which value of kernel.randomize_va_space enables full ASLR, heap (brk) included?","e":"0 disables ASLR, 1 randomizes stack, mmap and VDSO, 2 adds heap (brk) randomization. Value 2 is the default on common distributions.","placeholder":"Value…","answers":["2"]},
  "Un score CVSS mesure le risque qu'une vulnérabilité fait peser sur ton organisation. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A CVSS score measures the risk a vulnerability poses to your organization.","e":"FIRST reminds us: CVSS measures technical severity, not risk. Risk also depends on exposure, real-world exploitation (KEV, EPSS) and the value of the affected assets."},
  "Sous Windows, Credential Guard protège principalement… ¦ Les mots de passe enregistrés dans Edge, chiffrés par DPAPI": {"q":"On Windows, Credential Guard mainly protects…","e":"Credential Guard moves derived secrets (NTLM hashes, Kerberos tickets) into an isolated process (LSAIso) protected by VBS, which blocks pass-the-hash via an LSASS dump.","a":["Passwords saved in Edge, encrypted by DPAPI","BitLocker recovery keys backed up in Entra ID","NTLM and Kerberos secrets in LSASS, isolated by virtualization (VBS)","The local SAM database, against offline copies of the disk"]},
  "Lesquelles sont des protections contre l'exploitation de failles mémoire intégrées à Windows ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ DEP (prévention de l'exécution des données)": {"q":"Which of these are memory-exploit protections built into Windows? (several answers)","e":"DEP forbids running code in data areas, ASLR makes addresses unpredictable and CFG checks the targets of indirect calls: they make exploitation much harder. SysMain is a preloading service for performance.","a":["DEP (Data Execution Prevention)","ASLR (Address Space Layout Randomization)","CFG (Control Flow Guard)","SysMain (formerly Superfetch)"]},
  "Quelle option de montage empêche l'exécution directe de binaires sur une partition comme /tmp ? ¦ nosuid": {"q":"Which mount option prevents the direct execution of binaries on a partition such as /tmp?","e":"noexec forbids running binaries on the partition. nosuid ignores setuid/setgid bits, nodev forbids interpreting device files: also useful, but for other risks.","a":["nosuid","noexec","nodev","nouser"]},
  "Cycle de vie d'une vulnérabilité en divulgation coordonnée, dans l'ordre : ¦ Découverte de la faille par un chercheur": {"q":"Lifecycle of a vulnerability under coordinated disclosure, in order:","e":"With coordinated disclosure, the vendor is notified privately and has time to fix before publication. NIST's NVD then enriches the published CVE record.","items":["Discovery of the vulnerability by a researcher","Private report to the vendor","Publication of the patch and the CVE record","Enrichment of the record in the NVD (CVSS score, CPE)"]},
  "Pour une liste blanche applicative robuste sous Windows, Microsoft recommande aujourd'hui… ¦ AppLocker, car un administrateur local ne peut pas le contourner": {"q":"For robust application allowlisting on Windows, Microsoft now recommends…","e":"Microsoft presents App Control for Business as the reference application control solution. AppLocker remains a defense-in-depth layer, SRP is obsolete and UAC is not a security boundary.","a":["AppLocker, because a local administrator cannot bypass it","Software Restriction Policies (SRP)","User Account Control (UAC)","App Control for Business (formerly WDAC), enforced down to the kernel"]},
  "Le guide d'hygiène informatique de l'ANSSI (version 2017) regroupe… ¦ 25 mesures": {"q":"The ANSSI computer hygiene guide (2017 version) groups together…","e":"The guide “Renforcer la sécurité de son système d'information en 42 mesures” is a hardening baseline (inventory, accounts, updates, segmentation…). It often serves as a reference for a first level of security.","a":["25 measures","12 measures","42 measures","100 measures"]}
});
